1
00:00:06,506 --> 00:00:07,424
<i>Won-young.</i>

2
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:09,092
<i>Yes?</i>

3
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:13,513
You can't trick me.

4
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:23,732
When I saw his initial reaction
after coming up,

5
00:00:23,815 --> 00:00:25,775
I knew he was lying

6
00:00:26,484 --> 00:00:27,360
almost immediately.

7
00:00:27,444 --> 00:00:29,571
Compared to when he first went down there

8
00:00:29,654 --> 00:00:32,907
<i>to give us the briefing</i>
<i>on the hidden mission,</i>

9
00:00:32,991 --> 00:00:36,411
<i>his expression and the look in his eyes</i>
<i>when he came up later</i>

10
00:00:36,494 --> 00:00:38,371
<i>were totally different.</i>

11
00:00:38,455 --> 00:00:40,540
He was scrambling.

12
00:00:40,623 --> 00:00:41,458
That's when I knew.

13
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:43,918
<i>I realized he was playing us.</i>

14
00:00:44,002 --> 00:00:47,881
<i>I was certain he was hiding something.</i>

15
00:00:50,675 --> 00:00:52,719
I didn't let on in front of the others.

16
00:00:54,929 --> 00:00:55,764
But I felt

17
00:00:56,306 --> 00:01:00,393
you weren't telling the whole truth.

18
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:06,232
It'll just make things difficult
if you lie.

19
00:01:09,569 --> 00:01:10,862
It's not about what you're hiding.

20
00:01:12,155 --> 00:01:13,948
Your eyes…

21
00:01:14,491 --> 00:01:16,534
I know we haven't known each other
for that long,

22
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:18,495
but during our time together,

23
00:01:18,578 --> 00:01:21,873
I've never seen such a helpless look
in your eyes before.

24
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:25,001
Yeah.

25
00:01:27,253 --> 00:01:30,256
I'm sure. I'm 90% certain.

26
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:32,592
- I feel like…
- You suspect he has a hidden motive?

27
00:01:32,675 --> 00:01:34,260
Don't you think
there might be something else?

28
00:01:34,344 --> 00:01:36,012
I mean, it would make sense.

29
00:01:36,096 --> 00:01:39,516
If a pardon's involved,
the curse can actually be an advantage.

30
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:41,643
But I don't think
the curse itself is a lie.

31
00:01:41,726 --> 00:01:44,062
- That could be his mission.
- Rather than just a curse?

32
00:01:44,145 --> 00:01:46,106
But he definitely seems out of it.

33
00:01:46,189 --> 00:01:49,400
Regardless, I think it's only right

34
00:01:49,484 --> 00:01:53,154
that the challenger
be rewarded for their success.

35
00:01:53,238 --> 00:01:57,575
Maybe he was given a task
where you get a penalty for failure

36
00:01:57,659 --> 00:01:59,369
and an advantage for success.

37
00:01:59,869 --> 00:02:02,705
So you're saying he left that part out?

38
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:04,666
- It's a possibility.
- It's possible that he did.

39
00:02:04,749 --> 00:02:06,709
At first, I fully believed him.

40
00:02:06,793 --> 00:02:07,669
But then,

41
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:10,964
<i>both Hyun-min and Dong-jae</i>
<i>suggested a different possibility.</i>

42
00:02:11,756 --> 00:02:12,966
When I heard them out,

43
00:02:14,259 --> 00:02:17,053
I began to suspect
that he didn't give us the whole truth.

44
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:20,181
On the other hand,

45
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:25,103
I thought that while Won-young
might've kept some details out,

46
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:30,441
he'd share everything with me
when we're alone.

47
00:02:30,525 --> 00:02:33,570
But I don't think
he'll just keep this to himself.

48
00:02:33,653 --> 00:02:35,029
If there is something else,

49
00:02:35,113 --> 00:02:38,032
I feel like he'll tell me
or a select group later on.

50
00:02:38,116 --> 00:02:39,868
If he does, I'll share with you all.

51
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:42,620
I don't know what it is,

52
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:46,708
but I don't think it's something
you can handle alone.

53
00:02:51,546 --> 00:02:53,131
You seem overwhelmed.

54
00:02:53,798 --> 00:02:56,885
You're free to share with me if you wish.

55
00:03:02,765 --> 00:03:04,642
I'm here for you if you wanna talk.

56
00:03:06,352 --> 00:03:07,729
Don't worry too much.

57
00:03:08,521 --> 00:03:09,772
There's always a way out.

58
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:15,778
- I think I'll have to
- Yeah?

59
00:03:15,862 --> 00:03:18,281
make some sort of decision
tomorrow morning.

60
00:03:19,157 --> 00:03:21,159
I'll let you know then.

61
00:03:21,993 --> 00:03:22,952
All right.

62
00:03:23,578 --> 00:03:24,537
Good work today.

63
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:29,292
- He's coming back.
- Right. Okay.

64
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:31,878
These Pieces, man…

65
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:41,930
This is nice.

66
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:43,681
Good job today.

67
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:46,392
This feels so nice.

68
00:03:46,476 --> 00:03:47,727
Oh my.

69
00:03:47,810 --> 00:03:49,687
I'm gonna sleep like a baby tonight.

70
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:54,692
Good night.

71
00:04:24,389 --> 00:04:28,309
<i>When I woke up, I noticed a cold draft</i>
<i>blowing in from somewhere.</i>

72
00:04:28,393 --> 00:04:31,521
<i>I'm not sure whether</i>
<i>it's because my bed's by the door,</i>

73
00:04:31,604 --> 00:04:33,564
but I didn't get much sleep last night.

74
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:34,857
So this is prison, huh?

75
00:04:36,442 --> 00:04:37,610
It's so cold.

76
00:04:42,156 --> 00:04:43,783
<i>I slept so well.</i>

77
00:04:43,866 --> 00:04:46,619
I guess I'm more suited to prison life
than I thought.

78
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:52,875
It's not bad.

79
00:04:53,501 --> 00:04:55,211
Really? Has the food been upgraded?

80
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:57,380
- It's pretty good.
- I've never tried prison food before.

81
00:05:01,509 --> 00:05:02,927
The guys up there
had pig's trotters last night,

82
00:05:03,011 --> 00:05:04,470
so they won't have much
of an appetite now.

83
00:05:05,805 --> 00:05:07,181
I bet they're just feeling queasy.

84
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:27,076
The food here is nice.

85
00:05:36,044 --> 00:05:39,589
I hope they won't walk above me
first thing in the morning.

86
00:05:43,551 --> 00:05:45,011
Let's eat.

87
00:05:50,558 --> 00:05:53,061
Did you wake up early
because you have a lot on your mind?

88
00:05:53,144 --> 00:05:54,228
No, not at all.

89
00:06:03,738 --> 00:06:04,781
Chicken breast?

90
00:06:04,864 --> 00:06:05,823
I see.

91
00:06:06,991 --> 00:06:08,117
Can I ask you a question?

92
00:06:09,118 --> 00:06:12,455
Regarding the curse,

93
00:06:12,538 --> 00:06:15,124
do you get something
if you manage to break it?

94
00:06:17,835 --> 00:06:18,961
Yeah.

95
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:20,088
You do?

96
00:06:20,671 --> 00:06:22,090
- What is it?
- That perk

97
00:06:22,965 --> 00:06:26,260
you can use to pull someone out of prison.

98
00:06:26,344 --> 00:06:27,553
That's what you get?

99
00:06:28,054 --> 00:06:29,639
But it's transferable.

100
00:06:30,431 --> 00:06:32,725
I can give it to someone else
and have them pull me out.

101
00:06:34,018 --> 00:06:35,436
So you definitely need to break it.

102
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:36,521
It can be reserved too.

103
00:06:36,604 --> 00:06:38,022
- As in, you can hold onto it?
- Yeah.

104
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:39,982
Dang, that's amazing.

105
00:06:40,066 --> 00:06:42,110
So I can just hand it over whenever.

106
00:06:43,861 --> 00:06:45,238
It's basically

107
00:06:46,155 --> 00:06:48,241
a get-out-of-jail-free card.

108
00:06:48,324 --> 00:06:49,575
Yeah, exactly.

109
00:06:59,502 --> 00:07:00,878
It's a lovely morning at 7:30 a.m.

110
00:07:01,546 --> 00:07:02,505
Good morning.

111
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:06,676
I can shower, right?

112
00:07:07,218 --> 00:07:09,345
Amazing. That's an office worker for you.

113
00:07:14,350 --> 00:07:15,726
Good morning, everyone.

114
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:17,979
Word on the street is that
you may have snored a bit.

115
00:07:18,646 --> 00:07:20,314
Yeah, I probably did.

116
00:07:21,065 --> 00:07:22,733
- Do you normally snore?
- Yes.

117
00:07:22,817 --> 00:07:26,571
I think I tend to snore a lot
when I'm tired.

118
00:07:26,654 --> 00:07:28,364
That's fine. Everyone's like that.

119
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:31,742
At first, I wasn't reading into it at all,
so I didn't suspect a thing.

120
00:07:31,826 --> 00:07:35,830
I just thought that he'd done a good job,
but something must've happened down there.

121
00:07:35,913 --> 00:07:38,040
I think if Won-young is hiding anything,

122
00:07:38,124 --> 00:07:40,501
it must mean that the reward
is valuable enough to do so.

123
00:07:40,585 --> 00:07:41,502
I mean,

124
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:44,338
I can more or less get behind it.

125
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:47,300
But honestly,
the fact that he went in there

126
00:07:47,383 --> 00:07:49,010
is a double-edged sword.

127
00:07:49,677 --> 00:07:54,307
He went in there
and walked out with exclusive intel.

128
00:07:54,390 --> 00:07:55,516
- That's an upside for him.
- Right.

129
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,435
When he decides to share it with us,

130
00:07:57,518 --> 00:07:59,854
- Would he share everything?
- can we trust everything?

131
00:07:59,937 --> 00:08:01,397
Right, we can't be sure.

132
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:04,984
- There was 200 million won on the line.
- Right.

133
00:08:05,067 --> 00:08:07,528
There's no way
they would've made it that simple.

134
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:09,822
- I do think there is something.
- Right.

135
00:08:10,406 --> 00:08:13,284
If he's holding onto exclusive intel,

136
00:08:13,367 --> 00:08:15,578
that could be a game changer.

137
00:08:15,661 --> 00:08:17,622
- But there's a silver lining.
- Which is?

138
00:08:17,705 --> 00:08:21,876
He's not someone
who'd feed us false intel.

139
00:08:22,376 --> 00:08:24,378
He could be hiding something.

140
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:26,881
I don't think he has the acting chops
to pull that off.

141
00:08:27,715 --> 00:08:29,842
I'm just not sure
how they're gonna play it.

142
00:08:31,135 --> 00:08:33,262
Hopefully, they'll accept us
with open arms.

143
00:08:33,346 --> 00:08:34,805
- The players in the living area?
- Yeah.

144
00:08:34,889 --> 00:08:36,766
They could end up doubling down.

145
00:08:37,892 --> 00:08:41,312
- But they couldn't have banded together.
- Right?

146
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:43,814
What alliances should we expect?

147
00:08:44,565 --> 00:08:45,900
XITSUH,

148
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:48,778
you'll be working
with Dong-min today, right?

149
00:08:48,861 --> 00:08:52,031
My plan A is probably the leech strategy.

150
00:08:53,866 --> 00:08:55,409
I'll try the leech strategy first.

151
00:08:55,493 --> 00:08:57,245
As soon as I get up there,

152
00:08:57,870 --> 00:08:59,372
I'll get a read on the power dynamics.

153
00:08:59,455 --> 00:09:02,542
- To get a feel for the situation?
- Yeah, I'll try to loop you in too.

154
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:04,669
<i>Right now, there are no alliances at all.</i>

155
00:09:04,752 --> 00:09:08,464
I don't see the five of us
banding together at this point.

156
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:11,509
There are quite a few people
up in the living area,

157
00:09:11,592 --> 00:09:13,302
so they're bound to split up
to some degree.

158
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:17,890
So it feels like the smarter play

159
00:09:17,974 --> 00:09:21,519
<i>would be to join one of those two sides.</i>

160
00:09:23,437 --> 00:09:24,647
Come with me, Won-young.

161
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:35,658
I shared this earlier at breakfast,
but you two missed it.

162
00:09:41,831 --> 00:09:45,167
- I've already been cursed.
- Right.

163
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:46,627
If I break that curse…

164
00:09:50,131 --> 00:09:51,882
I get a token.

165
00:09:51,966 --> 00:09:54,885
It's called something like
an ascension talisman or a talisman token.

166
00:09:54,969 --> 00:09:56,846
It's a token that'll allow me

167
00:09:56,929 --> 00:09:58,848
to escape prison
and go to the living area.

168
00:09:58,931 --> 00:10:00,391
I can give it to someone else

169
00:10:01,183 --> 00:10:02,268
or use it myself.

170
00:10:04,103 --> 00:10:06,230
What do you need to do to break the curse?

171
00:10:07,315 --> 00:10:09,400
Get two people eliminated,
as you mentioned yesterday?

172
00:10:09,483 --> 00:10:10,401
Yeah.

173
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:15,114
Are you talking about something important?

174
00:10:15,197 --> 00:10:18,409
- No, we're not.
- We were talking about the curse.

175
00:10:18,492 --> 00:10:22,121
I didn't mention the advantage I'd get
if the curse were broken.

176
00:10:22,204 --> 00:10:24,665
- So I shared it over breakfast.
- I see.

177
00:10:25,499 --> 00:10:26,334
Yeah.

178
00:10:34,634 --> 00:10:35,843
Is this right?

179
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:38,679
It feels like I'm making
the wrinkles look worse.

180
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:45,770
Shall I try on the button-down?

181
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:47,688
I should tuck it in.

182
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:48,731
- Right.
- Okay.

183
00:10:48,814 --> 00:10:50,608
If you're worried
about your belly showing.

184
00:10:50,691 --> 00:10:51,525
Belly?

185
00:10:52,109 --> 00:10:53,569
I've never worried about that.

186
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:55,529
Tuck?

187
00:10:56,364 --> 00:10:57,323
No tuck?

188
00:10:57,948 --> 00:10:59,742
- No tuck.
- No tuck.

189
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:01,786
- Does it look all right?
- Yeah, you look good.

190
00:11:01,869 --> 00:11:02,745
- I'm glad.
- It suits you.

191
00:11:03,287 --> 00:11:04,121
That's good.

192
00:11:04,705 --> 00:11:06,791
Looks like the players in the living area
get a new outfit.

193
00:11:06,874 --> 00:11:08,584
- Yeah, they do.
- For the game?

194
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:11,545
They're glowing.

195
00:11:12,546 --> 00:11:15,424
- They're probably in better shape than us.
- That's for sure.

196
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:17,677
One thing's for certain.

197
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:19,720
- That outfit makes you look weak.
- Yeah.

198
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:21,222
- Super weak.
- Yeah.

199
00:11:21,305 --> 00:11:23,224
Finally, I can feel superior to them.

200
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:26,936
This prison uniform is nice.

201
00:11:35,569 --> 00:11:36,737
Let's team up.

202
00:11:39,281 --> 00:11:41,701
<i>The way I see it,</i>
<i>if we're playing a new game today,</i>

203
00:11:41,784 --> 00:11:44,286
<i>we're back at zero anyway.</i>

204
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:46,789
I'd say there's a chance

205
00:11:46,872 --> 00:11:49,291
we end up back on the same team.

206
00:11:49,375 --> 00:11:50,918
I'm keeping that door open.

207
00:11:51,919 --> 00:11:53,546
Let's do what we discussed yesterday.

208
00:11:53,629 --> 00:11:55,423
- Four of you.
- The four-three alliance.

209
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:57,299
- Four on one side, three on the other.
- Yeah.

210
00:11:57,383 --> 00:12:00,636
- And XITSUH?
- If he agrees to join us…

211
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:03,097
How are they looking down there?

212
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:06,392
There are five of them,
but no one's really taking the lead.

213
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:09,186
I don't think the five of them
will band together.

214
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:13,023
- If XITSUH doesn't rally those guys,
- Yeah.

215
00:12:13,107 --> 00:12:15,776
- they won't be banding together.
- Right.

216
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:18,404
Could we maybe just make one pact?

217
00:12:18,487 --> 00:12:20,614
If you're gonna deceive
and betray the rest of us,

218
00:12:20,698 --> 00:12:21,866
at least do it with style.

219
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:24,326
Make it look impressive.

220
00:12:24,410 --> 00:12:27,204
Make it look like
we had no choice but to fall for it.

221
00:12:28,289 --> 00:12:29,290
Make it dramatic.

222
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:33,878
<i>The main match will begin shortly.</i>

223
00:12:33,961 --> 00:12:36,922
<i>Everyone, please make your way</i>
<i>to the game area.</i>

224
00:12:40,217 --> 00:12:42,011
It's finally open.

225
00:12:42,094 --> 00:12:43,429
- Let's go.
- Good luck.

226
00:12:43,512 --> 00:12:44,555
- Let's go.
- We got this.

227
00:12:44,638 --> 00:12:46,390
- Good luck.
- We can do this.

228
00:12:46,474 --> 00:12:47,683
See you in the living area.

229
00:12:47,767 --> 00:12:48,934
Let's try our best.

230
00:12:49,643 --> 00:12:50,478
Good luck.

231
00:12:50,561 --> 00:12:51,645
Hello.

232
00:12:53,689 --> 00:12:54,857
Let's go, everyone.

233
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:56,400
We head out as soon as the bell rings?

234
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:57,902
- Everyone!
- Hello.

235
00:12:57,985 --> 00:12:58,986
Hello, neighbors.

236
00:13:00,821 --> 00:13:02,698
- Hello.
- Hello.

237
00:13:02,782 --> 00:13:03,991
Did you all sleep well?

238
00:13:04,074 --> 00:13:05,826
- Hello.
- How'd you sleep?

239
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:07,161
Are you aspiring chefs now?

240
00:13:07,244 --> 00:13:08,245
"Aspiring chefs"?

241
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:10,664
- You look like the White Spoons.
- You look so smart.

242
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:12,208
Upstairs looked very fancy.

243
00:13:12,291 --> 00:13:15,336
- Hello.
- We're gonna grab a bite first.

244
00:13:15,419 --> 00:13:16,754
We're still very hungry.

245
00:13:18,005 --> 00:13:19,006
Is there food?

246
00:13:20,090 --> 00:13:21,926
- No coffee?
- There's pizza.

247
00:13:22,009 --> 00:13:23,552
- Amazing.
- Pizza?

248
00:13:23,636 --> 00:13:25,054
Goodness gracious.

249
00:13:26,555 --> 00:13:27,556
Straight into your mouth.

250
00:13:34,814 --> 00:13:35,981
It's good.

251
00:13:36,065 --> 00:13:37,566
Sodium is so nice.

252
00:13:37,650 --> 00:13:39,276
The sodium did its magic.

253
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:40,945
I got so happy from a slice of pizza.

254
00:13:41,028 --> 00:13:42,112
That's the stuff.

255
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:44,365
Sodium is so nice.

256
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:47,159
- Good job hanging in there.
- It was nothing.

257
00:13:48,035 --> 00:13:49,370
Dong-min.

258
00:13:49,453 --> 00:13:50,496
Must've been tough down there.

259
00:13:50,579 --> 00:13:51,789
I wanna go upstairs.

260
00:13:52,289 --> 00:13:53,249
Of course.

261
00:13:53,332 --> 00:13:54,166
You will.

262
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:56,168
How's teamwork looking?

263
00:13:56,252 --> 00:13:58,170
Have the players
in the living area bonded?

264
00:13:58,254 --> 00:14:00,714
I'm not so sure about that.

265
00:14:00,798 --> 00:14:02,758
- Really?
- Did anything worth mentioning happen?

266
00:14:02,842 --> 00:14:05,928
<i>The players in the living area</i>
<i>have acquired prize tokens.</i>

267
00:14:07,096 --> 00:14:09,515
<i>Please insert the prize tokens</i>
<i>into their slots.</i>

268
00:14:09,598 --> 00:14:11,559
So those are the slots for the tokens.

269
00:14:11,642 --> 00:14:14,186
- There they are.
- This?

270
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:15,271
Two?

271
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:17,356
- You managed to secure two?
- Yeah.

272
00:14:18,983 --> 00:14:20,693
I guess Won-young secured them.

273
00:14:27,199 --> 00:14:28,492
Oh, that's cool. It lights up.

274
00:14:28,576 --> 00:14:29,618
Amazing.

275
00:14:30,452 --> 00:14:31,287
That's amazing.

276
00:14:32,705 --> 00:14:35,082
<i>200 million won has been added</i>
<i>to the prize money.</i>

277
00:14:37,751 --> 00:14:38,919
It's like <i>Squid Game</i>.

278
00:14:39,003 --> 00:14:40,045
So you got your wish.

279
00:14:40,129 --> 00:14:42,339
- I did it for the communal pot.
- How'd you do it?

280
00:14:42,423 --> 00:14:44,508
We gathered 12 Pieces.

281
00:14:45,009 --> 00:14:46,677
It was like a cast puzzle.

282
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:48,888
And you solved that on the first day?

283
00:14:48,971 --> 00:14:51,181
<i>The current final prize</i>
<i>stands at 200 million won.</i>

284
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:52,224
Great.

285
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:56,604
<i>We will now begin</i>
<i>the second main match of </i>The Devil's Plan.

286
00:14:57,229 --> 00:14:58,856
<i>After yesterday's prison match,</i>

287
00:14:58,939 --> 00:15:01,734
<i>Stella Jang and Hong Jin-ho</i>
<i>were eliminated.</i>

288
00:15:01,817 --> 00:15:04,737
<i>There are now 12 players remaining.</i>

289
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:06,238
<i>Before the game begins,</i>

290
00:15:06,322 --> 00:15:09,366
<i>here is the current Piece count</i>
<i>for each player.</i>

291
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:14,204
<i>Currently, Jang Dong-min</i>
<i>and Ha Seok-jin hold the most Pieces.</i>

292
00:15:14,872 --> 00:15:15,706
- Five.
- Five.

293
00:15:16,373 --> 00:15:17,458
That's humbling.

294
00:15:17,541 --> 00:15:21,086
<i>Now, let me introduce</i>
<i>the second main match.</i>

295
00:15:21,170 --> 00:15:22,046
Starting straight away.

296
00:15:22,129 --> 00:15:23,547
<i>Today's main match is</i>

297
00:15:23,631 --> 00:15:25,257
<i>Mystery Stock Market.</i>

298
00:15:25,341 --> 00:15:27,635
- Stocks.
- Stocks.

299
00:15:27,718 --> 00:15:28,802
<i>In Mystery Stock Market,</i>

300
00:15:28,886 --> 00:15:32,181
<i>players must figure out</i>
<i>the hidden rules of the stock market</i>

301
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:34,058
<i>to achieve the highest return.</i>

302
00:15:34,141 --> 00:15:35,684
I prefer long-term investment.

303
00:15:35,768 --> 00:15:36,685
Me too.

304
00:15:36,769 --> 00:15:37,978
- That's the way to go, right?
- Yeah.

305
00:15:38,062 --> 00:15:42,983
<i>Mystery Stock Market features</i>
<i>a total of seven company stocks.</i>

306
00:15:43,067 --> 00:15:46,111
<i>Every stock will open at 10,000 won,</i>

307
00:15:46,195 --> 00:15:50,908
<i>and the floor price</i>
<i>will be set at 100 won.</i>

308
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:53,494
<i>Each player will start the game</i>

309
00:15:53,577 --> 00:15:57,456
<i>with a personal device</i>
<i>and 100,000 won in virtual cash.</i>

310
00:15:57,539 --> 00:15:58,624
Every man for himself, huh?

311
00:15:58,707 --> 00:16:03,754
<i>The game consists of a total of 24 rounds,</i>
<i>with each round lasting 5 minutes.</i>

312
00:16:03,837 --> 00:16:05,881
- That's fast-paced.
- Five minutes?

313
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:07,758
<i>In every round,</i>
<i>players can use their device</i>

314
00:16:07,841 --> 00:16:09,969
<i>to buy and sell stocks of their choice,</i>

315
00:16:10,052 --> 00:16:15,683
<i>and they can also track their holdings</i>
<i>and each stock's live price in real time.</i>

316
00:16:16,558 --> 00:16:19,853
<i>Each round will flow</i>
<i>directly into the next,</i>

317
00:16:19,937 --> 00:16:24,942
<i>with updated stock prices,</i>
<i>trade status, total holdings,</i>

318
00:16:25,025 --> 00:16:30,030
<i>and player assets and rankings</i>
<i>displayed on the monitor at the start.</i>

319
00:16:30,114 --> 00:16:33,075
<i>Total holdings</i>
<i>refer to the total number of shares</i>

320
00:16:33,158 --> 00:16:37,037
<i>of a given stock that players</i>
<i>have purchased and are holding.</i>

321
00:16:37,121 --> 00:16:41,250
<i>Every stock in the exchange</i>
<i>has its own price fluctuation rules.</i>

322
00:16:41,333 --> 00:16:44,837
<i>Stock prices will fluctuate every round</i>
<i>according to these rules,</i>

323
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:49,633
<i>and only a part of each rule</i>
<i>will be revealed when the game begins.</i>

324
00:16:49,717 --> 00:16:53,679
<i>At the start of Rounds 5, 10, and 15,</i>

325
00:16:53,762 --> 00:16:56,390
<i>hidden parts of the rules</i>
<i>will be revealed one by one.</i>

326
00:16:56,473 --> 00:16:59,560
<i>At Round 20,</i>
<i>the rules will be fully disclosed.</i>

327
00:17:01,103 --> 00:17:04,481
<i>Sections highlighted in a different color</i>

328
00:17:04,565 --> 00:17:06,775
<i>indicate what will be revealed next.</i>

329
00:17:06,859 --> 00:17:09,528
<i>Additionally, players can use</i>
<i>a secret on a single stock</i>

330
00:17:09,611 --> 00:17:12,573
<i>only once throughout the game.</i>

331
00:17:12,656 --> 00:17:13,949
To hide information, I guess.

332
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:15,367
<i>Activating a secret</i>

333
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:18,704
<i>will hide that stock's price,</i>
<i>trading activity, and total holdings</i>

334
00:17:18,787 --> 00:17:23,459
<i>from other players for two rounds.</i>

335
00:17:23,542 --> 00:17:26,503
<i>For example,</i>
<i>if a secret is used in Round 2,</i>

336
00:17:26,587 --> 00:17:30,257
<i>its effect applies in Rounds 3 and 4.</i>

337
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:34,928
<i>However, if multiple players use a secret</i>
<i>on the same stock simultaneously,</i>

338
00:17:35,012 --> 00:17:37,097
<i>the effect applies only once,</i>

339
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:39,767
<i>and all secrets used will be consumed.</i>

340
00:17:39,850 --> 00:17:41,435
That's gonna get really messy.

341
00:17:41,518 --> 00:17:43,395
<i>While a secret is active,</i>

342
00:17:43,479 --> 00:17:45,731
<i>player rankings will be visible,</i>

343
00:17:45,814 --> 00:17:48,233
<i>but individual asset holdings</i>
<i>will not be disclosed.</i>

344
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:50,652
<i>At any point during the game,</i>

345
00:17:50,736 --> 00:17:54,239
<i>players can spend one Piece</i>
<i>to select one stock</i>

346
00:17:54,323 --> 00:17:57,659
<i>and preview the part of the rule</i>
<i>that will be revealed next.</i>

347
00:17:58,285 --> 00:17:59,745
So you're battling with Pieces.

348
00:17:59,828 --> 00:18:04,208
<i>Players can also exchange 1 Piece</i>
<i>for 10,000 won in virtual cash.</i>

349
00:18:04,708 --> 00:18:08,796
<i>However, Pieces can only be used</i>
<i>before Round 20 ends.</i>

350
00:18:08,879 --> 00:18:10,089
Round 20.

351
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:12,508
<i>The game will conclude</i>
<i>once all 24 rounds are completed</i>

352
00:18:12,591 --> 00:18:13,842
<i>in the same manner.</i>

353
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:18,514
<i>Trades made in Round 24 will be included</i>
<i>in the final total assets calculation.</i>

354
00:18:18,597 --> 00:18:20,390
<i>Based on the results,</i>

355
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:22,893
<i>players in first through fourth place</i>
<i>will go to the living area,</i>

356
00:18:22,976 --> 00:18:25,771
<i>and players in fifth through eleventh</i>
<i>will go to prison.</i>

357
00:18:25,854 --> 00:18:28,482
<i>The lowest-ranked player</i>
<i>will be eliminated.</i>

358
00:18:28,565 --> 00:18:31,652
<i>If there is a tie for last place,</i>

359
00:18:31,735 --> 00:18:36,323
<i>the player who had the lowest total assets</i>
<i>during the game will be eliminated.</i>

360
00:18:36,406 --> 00:18:37,699
- I can't go low.
- <i>Additionally,</i>

361
00:18:37,783 --> 00:18:39,701
<i>based on the final total assets,</i>

362
00:18:39,785 --> 00:18:42,704
<i>players with 1.5 million won or more</i>
<i>will receive 1 Piece,</i>

363
00:18:42,788 --> 00:18:45,374
<i>players with three million won or more</i>
<i>will receive two Pieces,</i>

364
00:18:45,457 --> 00:18:49,002
<i>and players with six million won or more</i>
<i>will receive three Pieces.</i>

365
00:18:49,795 --> 00:18:53,507
<i>If any player reaches</i>
<i>ten million won or more in assets,</i>

366
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:55,551
<i>a prize token will be given.</i>

367
00:18:56,593 --> 00:18:57,553
<i>The top-ranking player</i>

368
00:18:57,636 --> 00:19:00,389
<i>will be rewarded with an advantage,</i>
<i>the alliance token.</i>

369
00:19:01,807 --> 00:19:03,142
- That's amazing.
- Quite a haul.

370
00:19:03,225 --> 00:19:08,313
<i>The alliance token can be used</i>
<i>to select a player bound for prison</i>

371
00:19:08,397 --> 00:19:10,607
<i>and bring them to the living area.</i>

372
00:19:10,691 --> 00:19:13,610
<i>The devices will now be handed out.</i>

373
00:19:16,613 --> 00:19:17,447
What's up?

374
00:19:18,574 --> 00:19:20,742
There's no mechanism here
to eliminate two people.

375
00:19:20,826 --> 00:19:22,202
Yeah, that threw me off too.

376
00:19:22,286 --> 00:19:23,787
<i>Back in the living area,</i>

377
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:28,667
Won-young said that two people
would need to be eliminated.

378
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:33,088
<i>But the conditions for two eliminations</i>
<i>weren't revealed at all in today's game.</i>

379
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:35,674
<i>This must mean</i>

380
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,926
Won-young has lied at some point.

381
00:19:38,802 --> 00:19:40,137
- Shindong.
- I'm here.

382
00:19:40,637 --> 00:19:41,513
PLACE ORDER

383
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:42,431
EXCHANGE ACCESS GRANTED

384
00:19:42,514 --> 00:19:43,473
All right.

385
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:45,767
"Banger Steel."
I hope the stocks are bangers.

386
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:48,187
How can you make 10 million
with 100,000 won?

387
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:51,106
<i>Getting 10 million</i>
<i>or more out of 100,000 won?</i>

388
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:54,568
That's kind of my specialty,
if I say so myself.

389
00:19:54,651 --> 00:19:56,528
You know I'm a day trading pro, right?

390
00:19:56,612 --> 00:19:58,030
- You are?
- Click, click.

391
00:19:58,113 --> 00:19:59,489
I made a lot of money back then.

392
00:19:59,573 --> 00:20:02,951
With accurate information
and the confidence to back it up,

393
00:20:03,035 --> 00:20:04,953
I think you can invest aggressively.

394
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:09,458
I used my <i>Society Game </i>winnings
to buy Bitcoin and made a killing.

395
00:20:09,541 --> 00:20:13,128
<i>I think I have a fundamental aptitude</i>
<i>for stocks and investments.</i>

396
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:16,590
<i>The game will begin in 30 minutes.</i>

397
00:20:16,673 --> 00:20:17,925
He must be lying, right?

398
00:20:18,842 --> 00:20:20,427
- He must be.
- It doesn't make sense.

399
00:20:21,178 --> 00:20:25,307
But there's no scenario
where two people get eliminated.

400
00:20:26,642 --> 00:20:27,601
I'm not sure.

401
00:20:31,438 --> 00:20:34,858
<i>I think Won-young and I</i>
<i>have grown a little closer,</i>

402
00:20:34,942 --> 00:20:36,985
and he definitely told me yesterday…

403
00:20:37,069 --> 00:20:40,113
If two players aren't eliminated tomorrow,

404
00:20:40,197 --> 00:20:41,156
I end up cursed.

405
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:42,532
Only a part of the rules.

406
00:20:45,369 --> 00:20:47,079
All revealed in Round 20.

407
00:20:48,664 --> 00:20:52,542
I'm starting to suspect that he's lying.

408
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:55,087
<i>I'm not sure.</i>
<i>I'll have to see, but something feels off.</i>

409
00:20:55,170 --> 00:20:57,923
It's weird. There's no way
two can be eliminated today.

410
00:20:58,006 --> 00:20:59,675
- I know, right?
- So--

411
00:20:59,758 --> 00:21:02,427
I actually straight-up asked
Won-young about it.

412
00:21:02,511 --> 00:21:05,222
I said, "Hey, it doesn't seem like
two people can get eliminated today."

413
00:21:05,305 --> 00:21:06,556
Then he changed the subject.

414
00:21:07,307 --> 00:21:10,394
- He acted a bit weird.
- Something's definitely off.

415
00:21:10,477 --> 00:21:11,853
For today,

416
00:21:12,980 --> 00:21:17,067
we thought that Dong-min, Dong-jae,
you, and I could work together.

417
00:21:17,734 --> 00:21:20,112
During our discussion last night
in the living area…

418
00:21:20,195 --> 00:21:23,323
At the very least, I have to help XITSUH
in tomorrow's games.

419
00:21:23,407 --> 00:21:26,493
If XITSUH agrees to join,
then it'll be an alliance of eight.

420
00:21:26,576 --> 00:21:32,165
I wanna do everything I can
to get XITSUH a good placement today.

421
00:21:32,249 --> 00:21:35,669
<i>So I think he'll be joining us.</i>

422
00:21:35,752 --> 00:21:38,088
Would you be interested
in working together today?

423
00:21:38,171 --> 00:21:39,339
- Yes, of course.
- Okay.

424
00:21:39,423 --> 00:21:42,301
Just a heads-up
about the discussion in the prison.

425
00:21:42,384 --> 00:21:44,177
Since there are seven of you guys
and just five of us,

426
00:21:44,261 --> 00:21:46,805
we decided to give up the rivalry
and split off to join you guys.

427
00:21:46,888 --> 00:21:48,181
That's what we agreed to do.

428
00:21:48,265 --> 00:21:50,934
How have the players in the living area
been reshuffled?

429
00:21:51,018 --> 00:21:53,353
We're the ones hoping to keep
the Jang-Oh Alliance in check.

430
00:21:53,437 --> 00:21:54,813
I see.

431
00:21:54,896 --> 00:21:56,023
I'm on board with that.

432
00:21:56,106 --> 00:21:59,693
Are the five players from prison
not sticking together?

433
00:21:59,776 --> 00:22:02,237
- We didn't make any sort of pact.
- So no pact?

434
00:22:02,321 --> 00:22:03,155
Really?

435
00:22:03,238 --> 00:22:07,492
So the alliance over there
has Dong-jae, Hyun-min, XITSUH…

436
00:22:07,576 --> 00:22:08,785
- XITSUH's there?
- They took him in?

437
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:11,246
- Yeah, they teamed up, so--
- I thought they would.

438
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:16,001
Since Seok-jin has a lot of Pieces,
how about we recruit him together?

439
00:22:16,084 --> 00:22:19,004
Dong-min's alliance and my group
of four players in the living area

440
00:22:19,087 --> 00:22:20,505
have agreed to join forces.

441
00:22:20,589 --> 00:22:22,758
That was the plan at the start,

442
00:22:22,841 --> 00:22:26,303
<i>but the players from prison</i>
<i>started to approach us.</i>

443
00:22:26,386 --> 00:22:28,972
We can bring in the players from prison…

444
00:22:29,056 --> 00:22:31,808
- Weren't we supposed to work with them?
- Should we just…

445
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:32,726
Hold on.

446
00:22:32,809 --> 00:22:35,437
- Let's team up with the prison guys.
- You think so?

447
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:39,608
We can just shut them out
from the information we get from Dong-min.

448
00:22:39,691 --> 00:22:40,734
- As in the players from prison.
- We could do that.

449
00:22:40,817 --> 00:22:43,320
- That would be best for the four of us.
- Yeah, it is.

450
00:22:43,403 --> 00:22:44,654
<i>Then I changed my mind.</i>

451
00:22:44,738 --> 00:22:47,324
If we bring in the players from prison,

452
00:22:47,407 --> 00:22:49,826
we'd know what's happening on both sides.

453
00:22:49,910 --> 00:22:54,498
Then the four of us
could navigate things pretty well.

454
00:22:54,581 --> 00:22:56,750
Hold on a second.

455
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:58,335
The players from prison are pushing

456
00:22:58,418 --> 00:23:00,754
- to join forces right now.
- Okay.

457
00:23:00,837 --> 00:23:02,756
Would it be better
to gather intel with them

458
00:23:02,839 --> 00:23:07,010
- and share information with you guys?
- That sounds better.

459
00:23:07,094 --> 00:23:08,136
- Would you prefer that?
- Yeah.

460
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:11,264
Then, we'll bring in as many as we can

461
00:23:11,348 --> 00:23:12,682
- and work together.
- That's better

462
00:23:12,766 --> 00:23:15,018
- because they'll use Pieces for intel.
- Right.

463
00:23:15,102 --> 00:23:16,770
- And we can share that with you.
- Exactly.

464
00:23:20,065 --> 00:23:20,941
So?

465
00:23:21,024 --> 00:23:22,734
- They agreed.
- Then we need to hurry.

466
00:23:22,818 --> 00:23:25,362
I think teaming up is the right call.

467
00:23:25,445 --> 00:23:29,074
When I mentioned it, they agreed,
as long as we share the intel.

468
00:23:29,157 --> 00:23:32,744
Shindong, you'll play an important role,
but you'll need to move quickly.

469
00:23:32,828 --> 00:23:34,204
- Okay.
- In terms of communication.

470
00:23:34,287 --> 00:23:35,497
How many are in your group?

471
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:37,124
- Nothing has been set yet.
- Right.

472
00:23:37,207 --> 00:23:39,167
- I mean--
- Let's discuss it first.

473
00:23:39,251 --> 00:23:42,087
Right now, Dong-min and Hyun-min
are working together again.

474
00:23:42,170 --> 00:23:46,758
We did go through a lot together,
but we were planning to split up today.

475
00:23:46,842 --> 00:23:48,593
- XITSUH was already set
- Oh, really?

476
00:23:48,677 --> 00:23:49,970
- to work with Dong-min anyway.
- Yeah.

477
00:23:50,053 --> 00:23:51,513
Because of that alliance,

478
00:23:51,596 --> 00:23:53,932
- If we're being honest--
- we've become leftovers.

479
00:23:54,015 --> 00:23:56,893
- With Dong-min and Hyun-min together,
- I know.

480
00:23:56,977 --> 00:24:00,814
the right move to beat them
would be to build up numbers.

481
00:24:00,897 --> 00:24:03,066
But this one doesn't feel like
a numbers game.

482
00:24:03,150 --> 00:24:05,360
- No, with more intel--
- If you have more intel…

483
00:24:05,444 --> 00:24:06,736
- You're in a better position.
- Right.

484
00:24:06,820 --> 00:24:08,655
They said all parts of the rules

485
00:24:08,738 --> 00:24:10,699
get revealed at Round 20, right?

486
00:24:10,782 --> 00:24:13,785
The key is getting the intel before that.
Once Round 20 starts…

487
00:24:13,869 --> 00:24:15,495
- It's an even playing ground.
- Exactly.

488
00:24:15,579 --> 00:24:17,497
The real power here is the secret.

489
00:24:17,581 --> 00:24:20,125
Don't use your secret
under any circumstances.

490
00:24:20,208 --> 00:24:23,211
Let's make the others use up theirs.

491
00:24:23,295 --> 00:24:27,340
<i>In rounds where a secret is active,</i>
<i>not only are the stock's details hidden,</i>

492
00:24:27,424 --> 00:24:30,594
<i>but each player's individual total assets</i>
<i>are also not revealed.</i>

493
00:24:30,677 --> 00:24:33,847
<i>Additionally, players who hold,</i>
<i>buy, or sell the affected stock</i>

494
00:24:33,930 --> 00:24:39,144
<i>cannot check their total asset value</i>
<i>or cash holdings on their own devices.</i>

495
00:24:39,227 --> 00:24:42,856
<i>Since each player</i>
<i>can only use a secret once,</i>

496
00:24:42,939 --> 00:24:46,067
<i>it must be used at the right moment</i>
<i>and with careful consideration.</i>

497
00:24:46,610 --> 00:24:51,323
Up until Round 5, you just have to
watch the trends and make guesses.

498
00:24:51,406 --> 00:24:53,492
So if you buy the information

499
00:24:53,575 --> 00:24:56,453
set to be revealed at Round 15
during Round 11,

500
00:24:56,536 --> 00:24:58,538
you can more or less figure out
what the rules are.

501
00:24:58,622 --> 00:25:00,207
We need to buy everything at Round 11.

502
00:25:00,290 --> 00:25:02,751
Is it better
to learn the information early on?

503
00:25:02,834 --> 00:25:05,837
We can't be sure of anything
based on these little bits of info.

504
00:25:05,921 --> 00:25:08,131
We should buy intel when we have
a reasonable read on the price

505
00:25:08,215 --> 00:25:11,009
and believe the next reveal
will give us the entire rule.

506
00:25:11,092 --> 00:25:12,594
That's when we buy it and use a secret.

507
00:25:12,677 --> 00:25:14,221
So not in Round 1.

508
00:25:14,304 --> 00:25:17,224
The best time to buy
is around Round 6 or 11.

509
00:25:17,307 --> 00:25:18,391
It depends on the situation.

510
00:25:18,475 --> 00:25:20,060
But we have more secrets than they do.

511
00:25:20,143 --> 00:25:23,021
We can make it impossible
for them to decode the rules.

512
00:25:23,104 --> 00:25:26,441
<i>We'll first quickly find clues</i>
<i>about the price movements.</i>

513
00:25:26,525 --> 00:25:29,361
Then we'll use a Piece if we must
to deduce the rules as fast as possible.

514
00:25:29,444 --> 00:25:33,406
The key is using the secret
to monopolize the information.

515
00:25:33,490 --> 00:25:35,408
Gain the advantage and cut the others out.

516
00:25:35,492 --> 00:25:37,661
I think that will be
an important strategy.

517
00:25:37,744 --> 00:25:42,249
So I'd say the person
who can deduce the rules faster will win.

518
00:25:42,874 --> 00:25:45,001
There are quite a few sections
with the same number of blocks.

519
00:25:45,085 --> 00:25:48,088
Those probably mention another stock.

520
00:25:48,171 --> 00:25:49,172
The name of the company.

521
00:25:49,256 --> 00:25:50,674
But the movement here

522
00:25:51,424 --> 00:25:52,968
isn't linear, is it?

523
00:25:53,051 --> 00:25:55,011
- It reacts to the market conditions.
- Of each moment.

524
00:25:55,095 --> 00:25:57,389
Right. What's more, in CoyoTech's case,

525
00:25:57,472 --> 00:26:00,559
one section mentions the buy volume,
so it changes depending on our situation.

526
00:26:00,642 --> 00:26:02,978
It can then have a ripple effect
on the whole market.

527
00:26:03,061 --> 00:26:05,188
So you could leverage
Banger Steel or Mucho Construction

528
00:26:05,272 --> 00:26:08,108
- to drive changes in Analog Electronics.
- That's right.

529
00:26:08,191 --> 00:26:10,819
It's not just about tracking the price.

530
00:26:10,902 --> 00:26:13,363
You need to track everything
from buying volume to total holdings.

531
00:26:13,446 --> 00:26:15,490
This is completely different
from regular stock trading.

532
00:26:15,574 --> 00:26:17,117
This operates within a fixed set of rules.

533
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:19,119
<i>It's a game of deduction.</i>

534
00:26:19,202 --> 00:26:21,705
That's how stocks are.

535
00:26:21,788 --> 00:26:24,416
Everything feeds into everything else.

536
00:26:24,499 --> 00:26:26,960
Construction and Steel
will be tied together.

537
00:26:27,544 --> 00:26:32,382
And CoyoTech and Analog Electronics
fall in the same category.

538
00:26:32,465 --> 00:26:35,218
They'll likely move
within a reasonable range.

539
00:26:35,719 --> 00:26:38,722
A construction company is most likely
to be affected by a steel company.

540
00:26:39,681 --> 00:26:41,099
"The price of Banger Steel…"

541
00:26:41,182 --> 00:26:42,976
It's a construction company,
at the end of the day.

542
00:26:43,059 --> 00:26:45,604
- "Price of Alt Ent."
- That'd be so random.

543
00:26:45,687 --> 00:26:48,106
It needs to make sense.

544
00:26:48,732 --> 00:26:51,484
- This one is definitely "otherwise."
- Right.

545
00:26:51,568 --> 00:26:57,240
For Open Security, the last part must be
something like "±1,000 won."

546
00:26:57,324 --> 00:26:59,242
But I'm clueless
about the part before that.

547
00:26:59,326 --> 00:27:00,577
- It can't be an amount.
- Percentage?

548
00:27:00,660 --> 00:27:01,661
It could be that.

549
00:27:01,745 --> 00:27:05,999
We've got -200 won,
+200 won, and +1,500 won.

550
00:27:06,082 --> 00:27:07,292
These are absolute changes.

551
00:27:07,375 --> 00:27:10,629
There's no way you can make
ten million won with absolute changes,

552
00:27:10,712 --> 00:27:12,505
so it'll come down to the growth rate.

553
00:27:12,589 --> 00:27:13,673
BANGER STEEL

554
00:27:13,757 --> 00:27:15,133
What's with this spacing?

555
00:27:15,216 --> 00:27:16,885
How can spacing like this even come up?

556
00:27:17,427 --> 00:27:19,554
I think it's "total holdings."

557
00:27:19,638 --> 00:27:22,140
- Something like, "X's total holdings."
- Right.

558
00:27:22,891 --> 00:27:25,727
And these two are in opposition
to each other.

559
00:27:26,311 --> 00:27:28,438
<i>Your time is up.</i>

560
00:27:28,521 --> 00:27:30,273
<i>Everyone, please gather in the hall.</i>

561
00:27:30,357 --> 00:27:32,192
<i>Round 1 will now begin.</i>

562
00:27:32,275 --> 00:27:34,694
<i>Please begin trading now.</i>

563
00:27:35,278 --> 00:27:36,613
- Are you gonna diversify?
- What?

564
00:27:36,696 --> 00:27:37,614
I mean your portfolio.

565
00:27:37,697 --> 00:27:38,782
I'm thinking about it.

566
00:27:40,408 --> 00:27:41,910
- Maybe just buy two?
- What?

567
00:27:41,993 --> 00:27:43,119
Maybe just buy two?

568
00:27:44,788 --> 00:27:45,789
Two?

569
00:27:45,872 --> 00:27:48,333
For now, I'm just teaming up
with a few people.

570
00:27:48,416 --> 00:27:51,878
We put in 10,000 won each
