603
00:28:59,362 --> 00:29:01,448
Maybe I should switch to Construction.

604
00:29:01,531 --> 00:29:03,950
- Did you go for Construction or Capital?
- Construction is one of the linked ones,

605
00:29:04,033 --> 00:29:05,827
- so it'll see fewer changes.
- Then Steel it is.

606
00:29:05,910 --> 00:29:06,745
That's good.

607
00:29:06,828 --> 00:29:08,496
You're not buying this round, right?

608
00:29:09,456 --> 00:29:10,373
I should observe first.

609
00:29:10,457 --> 00:29:12,667
- Don't buy anything yet.
- That's my plan.

610
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:15,211
Diversify individually first,

611
00:29:15,295 --> 00:29:17,255
and when the information
starts to come together,

612
00:29:17,338 --> 00:29:19,507
<i>that's when we can make our move.</i>

613
00:29:20,842 --> 00:29:22,051
Here's my guess for this one.

614
00:29:22,135 --> 00:29:25,054
If the price goes up or down,
then it sees an X% spike or drop.

615
00:29:25,138 --> 00:29:26,890
I think the next two blocks are,
"if unchanged."

616
00:29:26,973 --> 00:29:27,807
Right.

617
00:29:27,891 --> 00:29:30,226
But considering the trends
in the stock market,

618
00:29:30,310 --> 00:29:33,229
the first block
of Mucho Construction's rule

619
00:29:33,313 --> 00:29:34,773
must mention Banger Steel.

620
00:29:34,856 --> 00:29:36,524
- Right, so another company's name.
- Yeah.

621
00:29:36,608 --> 00:29:37,609
So, if X's price…

622
00:29:37,692 --> 00:29:38,818
If you ask me,

623
00:29:39,444 --> 00:29:41,112
we need the verb "changes."

624
00:29:41,196 --> 00:29:43,740
- "If it changes, X%, if not--"
- No, not necessarily.

625
00:29:43,823 --> 00:29:45,366
Think about possible changes.

626
00:29:45,450 --> 00:29:48,495
- Like "rise"?
- It can rise or fall.

627
00:29:48,578 --> 00:29:50,205
- That's possible.
- But my guess is "rise."

628
00:29:50,288 --> 00:29:51,247
It could be something like,

629
00:29:51,331 --> 00:29:53,082
"If Banger Steel's price

630
00:29:53,833 --> 00:29:56,461
rises, +10%."

631
00:29:56,544 --> 00:29:59,923
- "If not, then -X%."
- "If not, then -X%"?

632
00:30:00,006 --> 00:30:03,092
I think we should be able to
crack this one the fastest.

633
00:30:03,176 --> 00:30:04,844
- This has to be "than," right?
- Right.

634
00:30:04,928 --> 00:30:06,679
It could be,
"If Analog Electronics' X is greater than

635
00:30:06,763 --> 00:30:08,765
- Buying volume for X.
- CoyoTech's buying volume…"

636
00:30:08,848 --> 00:30:10,725
The latter part
will talk about the price change.

637
00:30:10,809 --> 00:30:13,603
- It has to be linked to Electronics.
- "If not."

638
00:30:13,686 --> 00:30:15,188
These blocks here in Mucho Construction,

639
00:30:15,271 --> 00:30:18,441
- CoyoTech, and Analog Electronics' rules
- "If not," right?

640
00:30:18,525 --> 00:30:20,985
all have to be "if not."

641
00:30:21,069 --> 00:30:23,112
It all comes down to information
like in real stock.

642
00:30:23,196 --> 00:30:24,197
It's a battle of information.

643
00:30:24,280 --> 00:30:29,494
<i>Even now, you can already get</i>
<i>a rough sense of things.</i>

644
00:30:29,577 --> 00:30:32,413
<i>So instead of going in aggressively,</i>

645
00:30:32,497 --> 00:30:35,041
<i>I'll be keeping an eye on the price</i>
<i>and a few other factors.</i>

646
00:30:35,124 --> 00:30:40,129
What would cause Banger Steel
to fall 200 or rise 200 won?

647
00:30:40,213 --> 00:30:45,760
- This rise or fall is the per-share price.
- Right. Per share.

648
00:30:45,844 --> 00:30:48,429
The ones with the most potential right now

649
00:30:48,513 --> 00:30:50,181
are Mucho Construction and Banger Steel.

650
00:30:50,265 --> 00:30:53,935
Would it be okay if I buy ten shares
