01:01:22,470 --> 01:01:23,429
- Who did it?
- Who did it?

1414
01:01:23,930 --> 01:01:25,098
Kyung-lyul.

1415
01:01:25,181 --> 01:01:26,099
He did?

1416
01:01:28,434 --> 01:01:29,727
Can I come in?

1417
01:01:29,811 --> 01:01:32,689
Should I buy Open Security this round?

1418
01:01:32,772 --> 01:01:35,608
Definitely, since we're using
a secret on Analog Electronics.

1419
01:01:36,317 --> 01:01:38,152
We haven't decided on that yet.

1420
01:01:38,236 --> 01:01:39,362
- You're not gonna?
- No.

1421
01:01:39,445 --> 01:01:41,239
I just bought Open Security.

1422
01:01:41,322 --> 01:01:43,616
- I don't think we should be sharing info.
- What?

1423
01:01:43,700 --> 01:01:46,661
It's us against them now.
We can't open up everything.

1424
01:01:46,744 --> 01:01:49,497
We're only sharing intel among ourselves.

1425
01:01:49,580 --> 01:01:51,040
Looks like they don't wanna share intel.

1426
01:01:51,124 --> 01:01:52,291
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

1427
01:01:52,375 --> 01:01:54,377
Can we trust they used a secret?

1428
01:01:54,460 --> 01:01:57,964
I think there's a good chance
Kyung-lyul using it was a lie.

1429
01:01:58,631 --> 01:02:00,591
Won-young, what's going on over there?

1430
01:02:00,675 --> 01:02:03,261
There's too much to deal with,
so I can't even look out for myself.

1431
01:02:04,137 --> 01:02:07,306
They won't go for Banger Steel this round.

1432
01:02:07,390 --> 01:02:09,517
They'll just take the 13% gains
from Open Security.

1433
01:02:09,600 --> 01:02:10,768
- With a secret?
- Yeah.

1434
01:02:10,852 --> 01:02:12,270
"The stock that falls the most…"

1435
01:02:12,353 --> 01:02:16,023
Or "If the stock that fell furthest
from the starting point rises…"

1436
01:02:16,107 --> 01:02:18,067
Then how do you explain the flat period?

1437
01:02:18,151 --> 01:02:21,195
- Is this about NotSoGood Capital?
- The most-dropped stock didn't rise.

1438
01:02:23,364 --> 01:02:25,199
I think Yurisa's prediction is right.

1439
01:02:25,283 --> 01:02:26,617
- What do you mean?
- Look.

1440
01:02:26,701 --> 01:02:28,745
So it's, "If the stock
that fell the most rises"

1441
01:02:28,828 --> 01:02:31,080
and "If the stock
that fell the most falls," right?

1442
01:02:31,164 --> 01:02:33,040
Look at Rounds 7 and 8.

1443
01:02:33,124 --> 01:02:35,543
The chart stayed flat
because Capital was the cheapest.

1444
01:02:35,626 --> 01:02:38,921
NotSoGood Capital was the cheapest,
so it stayed flat.

1445
01:02:39,005 --> 01:02:42,967
Then, Construction dropped the most
to become the biggest decliner.

1446
01:02:43,050 --> 01:02:46,137
And Mucho Construction fell further
when it was already the cheapest.

1447
01:02:46,220 --> 01:02:49,182
Because Mucho Construction dropped,
the 10% decline in Capital started again.

1448
01:02:49,265 --> 01:02:50,308
<i>You have one minute left.</i>

1449
01:02:50,391 --> 01:02:54,353
So if Mucho Construction rises now,
NotSoGood Capital will rise 20%.

1450
01:02:55,229 --> 01:02:57,231
- And Mucho Construction is gonna rise.
- Yeah.

1451
01:02:57,315 --> 01:02:58,566
- Is it?
- Yeah.

1452
01:02:58,649 --> 01:03:00,234
If you sell.

1453
01:03:00,318 --> 01:03:04,155
<i>If Yurisa's deduction</i>
<i>on NotSoGood Capital's rule is correct,</i>

1454
01:03:04,238 --> 01:03:06,240
<i>they need to raise the price</i>
<i>of Mucho Construction,</i>

1455
01:03:06,324 --> 01:03:08,576
<i>which is currently the cheapest stock.</i>

1456
01:03:08,659 --> 01:03:10,745
<i>To raise the price of Mucho Construction,</i>

1457
01:03:10,828 --> 01:03:13,915
<i>they need to raise Banger Steel's price</i>
<i>by even just one won.</i>

1458
01:03:13,998 --> 01:03:17,835
<i>To raise the price of Banger Steel,</i>
<i>they need to reduce its total holdings.</i>

1459
01:03:17,919 --> 01:03:20,838
<i>Yurisa currently holds</i>
<i>one share of Banger Steel.</i>

1460
01:03:20,922 --> 01:03:23,841
<i>If she reduces</i>
<i>the two-share total holdings to one,</i>

1461
01:03:23,925 --> 01:03:26,093
<i>Banger Steel's price will rise,</i>

1462
01:03:26,177 --> 01:03:29,013
<i>which will cause</i>
<i>Mucho Construction's price to rise.</i>

1463
01:03:29,096 --> 01:03:33,601
<i>As a result,</i>
<i>NotSoGood Capital's stock will rise 20%.</i>

1464
01:03:34,560 --> 01:03:37,647
That's assuming it goes through.
I've only got one share.

1465
01:03:37,730 --> 01:03:38,940
There are just two shares--

1466
01:03:39,023 --> 01:03:41,567
Then let's test it and use a secret
on NotSoGood Capital in the next round.

1467
01:03:41,651 --> 01:03:42,819
You should sell first.

1468
01:03:42,902 --> 01:03:44,111
- I did.
- You did?

1469
01:03:44,195 --> 01:03:45,071
Already?

1470
01:03:45,154 --> 01:03:46,614
- Then the other team--
- We used a secret anyway.

1471
01:03:46,697 --> 01:03:48,950
<i>That concludes Round 12.</i>

1472
01:03:49,033 --> 01:03:51,160
<i>Round 13 will now begin.</i>

1473
01:03:51,244 --> 01:03:53,955
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

1474
01:03:54,872 --> 01:03:56,833
- It's the same?
- The buy and sell counts were one each.

1475
01:03:56,916 --> 01:03:59,377
Someone over there bought one.

1476
01:03:59,460 --> 01:04:01,337
- We sold one, and they bought one?
- Yeah.

1477
01:04:01,420 --> 01:04:02,880
They canceled each other out.

1478
01:04:02,964 --> 01:04:05,299
But the most-dropped stock,
Mucho Construction, dropped,

1479
01:04:05,383 --> 01:04:06,217
so Capital is declining.

1480
01:04:06,300 --> 01:04:09,011
- I think the "most-dropped" part is right.
- You're right.

1481
01:04:09,095 --> 01:04:10,471
- We can go all in.
- We figured it out.

1482
01:04:10,555 --> 01:04:13,683
To raise Mucho Construction,
we need to raise Banger Steel.

1483
01:04:13,766 --> 01:04:17,144
And to raise Banger Steel,
we have to use a secret

1484
01:04:17,228 --> 01:04:19,313
so they can't see how many we've bought.

1485
01:04:19,397 --> 01:04:20,940
Then we sell everything.

1486
01:04:21,023 --> 01:04:24,193
I told them I used my secret,
so they'll probably go for Open Security.

1487
01:04:24,277 --> 01:04:27,780
Can't we sell Banger Steel now
and get 20% on Capital in the next round?

1488
01:04:27,864 --> 01:04:29,866
We can't raise Banger Steel.
We don't have any.

1489
01:04:29,949 --> 01:04:31,325
- They have two--
- Didn't you have one?

1490
01:04:31,409 --> 01:04:32,410
- She sold it.
- I just sold it.

1491
01:04:32,493 --> 01:04:33,953
- Why did you sell it?
- And they bought another one.

1492
01:04:34,036 --> 01:04:36,747
They have two shares
of Banger Steel right now.

1493
01:04:36,831 --> 01:04:37,999
We should've bought some.

1494
01:04:38,082 --> 01:04:39,917
We should buy some this round.

1495
01:04:40,001 --> 01:04:41,794
Yeah, we need to do that this round.

1496
01:04:41,878 --> 01:04:43,713
Everyone needs to buy Banger Steel,
even if only a few.

1497
01:04:43,796 --> 01:04:45,923
- Right, we just need more than them.
- Got it.

1498
01:04:46,007 --> 01:04:47,091
- Just one each?
- Yes.

1499
01:04:47,174 --> 01:04:48,676
I'll buy one too.

1500
01:04:49,302 --> 01:04:50,803
Once we see them rise,

1501
01:04:50,887 --> 01:04:53,431
let's slap a secret on Banger Steel
and NotSoGood Capital right away.

1502
01:04:53,514 --> 01:04:55,725
We need to do it this round.
They can't see how many we bought.

1503
01:04:55,808 --> 01:04:57,560
- We have to do it now.
- Should I do it now?

1504
01:04:57,643 --> 01:04:58,978
- I'll do it now.
- Okay.

1505
01:04:59,061 --> 01:05:00,104
BANGER STEEL
SECRET

1506
01:05:00,187 --> 01:05:02,523
- We also need to think about Alt Ent.
- Right.

1507
01:05:02,607 --> 01:05:04,400
- Its price has been dropping.
- It's an enigma.

1508
01:05:04,483 --> 01:05:06,235
I just can't figure it out.

1509
01:05:06,319 --> 01:05:08,070
I even paid for a clue. How frustrating.

1510
01:05:08,154 --> 01:05:09,739
Who bought Banger Steel?

1511
01:05:09,822 --> 01:05:11,282
- I bought one.
- Me too.

1512
01:05:11,365 --> 01:05:13,117
Then we have four, right? Okay.

1513
01:05:13,200 --> 01:05:15,328
I found a guaranteed winning strategy.

1514
01:05:17,788 --> 01:05:20,666
We can each put in 120,000 won

1515
01:05:20,750 --> 01:05:23,169
to send Banger Steel down
to the 100-won floor right away.

1516
01:05:23,252 --> 01:05:28,257
Then, we'll each buy 180,000 won worth
and hold for a round. It's still 100 won.

1517
01:05:28,341 --> 01:05:31,135
When we make the second investment,
each share will cost only 100 won,

1518
01:05:31,218 --> 01:05:32,762
when each initially cost 10,000 won.

1519
01:05:32,845 --> 01:05:34,764
- But--
- When the four of us

1520
01:05:34,847 --> 01:05:38,726
sell 120,000 won worth together,
the price goes back to 10,000 won.

1521
01:05:38,809 --> 01:05:43,481
Since we used 180,000 won to buy
100-won shares, we'd have 1,800 of them.

1522
01:05:43,564 --> 01:05:44,815
At 10,000 won, that's…

1523
01:05:44,899 --> 01:05:47,109
<i>This is XITSUH's strategy.</i>

1524
01:05:47,193 --> 01:05:48,361
<i>Using Banger Steel's rule,</i>

1525
01:05:48,444 --> 01:05:51,155
<i>where the price falls</i>
<i>as total holdings increase,</i>

1526
01:05:51,238 --> 01:05:52,698
<i>the team buys Banger Steel shares</i>

1527
01:05:52,782 --> 01:05:55,576
<i>so the total holdings</i>
<i>between them reach 50.</i>

1528
01:05:55,660 --> 01:05:58,537
<i>As a result,</i>
<i>Banger Steel's price of 9,600 won</i>

1529
01:05:58,621 --> 01:06:00,998
<i>falls to the floor price of 100 won.</i>

1530
01:06:01,582 --> 01:06:04,710
<i>In the following round,</i>
<i>they invest all remaining assets</i>

1531
01:06:04,794 --> 01:06:07,088
<i>to buy up Banger Steel shares at 100 won.</i>

1532
01:06:07,171 --> 01:06:10,341
<i>At this point,</i>
<i>Banger Steel's total holdings increase,</i>

1533
01:06:10,424 --> 01:06:14,220
<i>but the price cannot go below 100 won.</i>

1534
01:06:14,303 --> 01:06:17,473
<i>If Jang Dong-min sells just 50 shares</i>
<i>in the next round,</i>

1535
01:06:17,556 --> 01:06:22,019
<i>Banger Steel's price rises by 10,000%.</i>

1536
01:06:22,103 --> 01:06:26,941
<i>Then, Jang Dong-min's total assets</i>
<i>will far exceed ten million won.</i>

1537
01:06:27,024 --> 01:06:29,110
There's only one way we can win right now.

1538
01:06:29,193 --> 01:06:32,071
Use the information
we obtained ahead of them

1539
01:06:32,154 --> 01:06:33,406
to take another gain.

1540
01:06:33,489 --> 01:06:35,282
For your plan to work,
they can't know about Steel.

1541
01:06:35,366 --> 01:06:36,534
But they do.

1542
01:06:36,617 --> 01:06:38,619
- Right, they know everything.
- They do.

1543
01:06:38,703 --> 01:06:41,455
So if we go through with that plan,
everyone will benefit.

1544
01:06:41,539 --> 01:06:43,541
<i>There were far too many ways</i>
<i>for it to go sideways.</i>

1545
01:06:43,624 --> 01:06:49,213
We considered whether it was worth
that kind of risk and decided against it.

1546
01:06:49,296 --> 01:06:51,424
It won't work
because they know all about it, right?

1547
01:06:51,507 --> 01:06:52,425
Yeah, they know everything.

1548
01:06:59,765 --> 01:07:02,685
MYSTERY STOCK MARKET

1549
01:07:08,733 --> 01:07:11,068
We need to buy CoyoTech this round
for a 14% return.

1550
01:07:11,152 --> 01:07:12,945
Open Security only gives you a 13% gain.

1551
01:07:13,029 --> 01:07:15,656
CoyoTech rises 1,400 won, which is 14%.

1552
01:07:16,198 --> 01:07:18,701
- CoyoTech then?
- Yeah, and we need to flip things fast.

1553
01:07:19,326 --> 01:07:21,078
- CoyoTech?
- Buy and sell CoyoTech.

1554
01:07:21,162 --> 01:07:22,121
Okay.

1555
01:07:22,204 --> 01:07:24,457
<i>That concludes Round 13.</i>

1556
01:07:24,540 --> 01:07:26,751
<i>Round 14 will now begin.</i>

1557
01:07:26,834 --> 01:07:29,295
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

1558
01:07:29,378 --> 01:07:30,212
BANGER STEEL

1559
01:07:30,296 --> 01:07:31,672
- A secret on Banger Steel?
- What the heck?

1560
01:07:31,756 --> 01:07:33,090
- They must be working on it.
- What's going on?

1561
01:07:33,174 --> 01:07:34,550
- They must be aiming for first.
- Look at that.

1562
01:07:34,633 --> 01:07:36,010
They went for CoyoTech.

1563
01:07:36,093 --> 01:07:37,303
3,150 SHARES BOUGHT, 3,022 SHARES SOLD

1564
01:07:37,386 --> 01:07:39,180
- CoyoTech went up.
- Yeah.

1565
01:07:39,263 --> 01:07:42,516
Let's use a secret on NotSoGood Capital
and go for Mucho Construction.

1566
01:07:42,600 --> 01:07:43,726
- Yeah, that's it.
- Yeah.

1567
01:07:43,809 --> 01:07:46,353
They bought Banger Steel.
They're running trades on it.

1568
01:07:46,437 --> 01:07:48,481
Buying it themselves
is the worst-case scenario.

1569
01:07:48,564 --> 01:07:49,398
No, hold on.

1570
01:07:49,482 --> 01:07:52,443
- Just a second. They have to go all in.
- Listen.

1571
01:07:52,526 --> 01:07:56,614
They just used a secret on Banger Steel
and bought its shares.

1572
01:07:56,697 --> 01:07:58,657
- They're going for NotSoGood Capital.
- What?

1573
01:07:58,741 --> 01:08:00,534
They're going for NotSoGood Capital
in the next round.

1574
01:08:00,618 --> 01:08:01,911
- I doubt it.
- I'm sure of it.

1575
01:08:01,994 --> 01:08:05,498
- They're after NotSoGood Capital.
- Capital will give them a 20% gain.

1576
01:08:05,581 --> 01:08:08,000
Can we earn more than they do?

1577
01:08:08,084 --> 01:08:09,668
Did we predict
NotSoGood Capital's rule right?

1578
01:08:09,752 --> 01:08:11,462
- I hope we did.
- We'll have to wait and see.

1579
01:08:11,545 --> 01:08:13,964
- We'll buy NotSoGood Capital--
- Do I sell everything and buy it?

1580
01:08:14,048 --> 01:08:15,883
- Yeah. Sell Banger Steel.
- Banger Steel.

1581
01:08:15,966 --> 01:08:17,301
Sell all Banger Steel.

1582
01:08:17,384 --> 01:08:19,011
Yeah, and buy NotSoGood Capital.

1583
01:08:19,512 --> 01:08:21,806
Sorry, but can I buy CoyoTech?

1584
01:08:21,889 --> 01:08:23,224
- Be our guest.
- Go ahead.

1585
01:08:23,307 --> 01:08:24,141
It's because I'm last.

1586
01:08:24,225 --> 01:08:26,060
We're all buying NotSoGood Capital, right?

1587
01:08:26,143 --> 01:08:28,771
- Yeah, and sell all Banger Steel.
- Okay.

1588
01:08:28,854 --> 01:08:30,606
And we need a secret on NotSoGood Capital.

1589
01:08:30,689 --> 01:08:31,774
- I can do it.
- Okay.

1590
01:08:31,857 --> 01:08:32,691
NOTSOGOOD CAPITAL
SECRET

1591
01:08:32,775 --> 01:08:34,735
<i>That concludes Round 14.</i>

1592
01:08:34,819 --> 01:08:38,114
- Let's see now.
<i>- Round 15 will now begin.</i>

1593
01:08:38,197 --> 01:08:39,240
Please.

1594
01:08:39,323 --> 01:08:41,575
- Please.
<i>- Round 15 will now begin.</i>

1595
01:08:41,659 --> 01:08:44,870
<i>Here are the stock rules.</i>

1596
01:08:49,416 --> 01:08:52,294
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

1597
01:08:52,378 --> 01:08:53,546
It went down.

1598
01:08:53,629 --> 01:08:55,464
MUCHO CONSTRUCTION: ▼2,794 WON

1599
01:08:55,548 --> 01:08:57,091
We're screwed.

1600
01:08:57,174 --> 01:08:59,635
If Mucho Construction dropped,
we failed, right?

1601
01:08:59,718 --> 01:09:01,053
- Yeah, we did.
- Yeah.

1602
01:09:01,137 --> 01:09:02,221
ALT ENT: ▼3,200 WON

1603
01:09:02,304 --> 01:09:04,390
ALT ENT: ▲5,000 WON

1604
01:09:04,473 --> 01:09:06,225
I think they know about Alt Ent.

1605
01:09:06,308 --> 01:09:08,519
What's it following? It just went back up.

1606
01:09:08,602 --> 01:09:10,729
They figured out Alt Ent's rule.

1607
01:09:11,397 --> 01:09:12,690
- Yeah.
- They already did.

1608
01:09:12,773 --> 01:09:14,316
Guess they're more observant than we are.

1609
01:09:14,400 --> 01:09:16,986
<i>The other team decoded</i>
<i>Alt Ent's rule before us.</i>

1610
01:09:17,069 --> 01:09:18,779
<i>That widened the gap drastically.</i>

1611
01:09:18,863 --> 01:09:20,531
<i>They had a sharp observer.</i>

1612
01:09:20,614 --> 01:09:25,703
Nobody bought or sold Alt Ent at all,
so I kept an eye on it.

1613
01:09:25,786 --> 01:09:28,330
<i>It just dropped and rose</i>
<i>without anyone doing anything to it.</i>

1614
01:09:28,414 --> 01:09:32,209
<i>It kept repeating that cycle,</i>
<i>and I couldn't figure it out.</i>

1615
01:09:32,293 --> 01:09:34,211
Come here.

1616
01:09:34,295 --> 01:09:37,047
- You see Alt Ent?
- Yes.

1617
01:09:37,131 --> 01:09:40,843
Do you see the graph
above "Mystery Stock Market"?

1618
01:09:40,926 --> 01:09:43,679
- Yes.
- That could be the same graph.

1619
01:09:43,762 --> 01:09:45,347
- I can see that.
- Yeah.

1620
01:09:47,099 --> 01:09:49,727
There are two low points marked there.

1621
01:09:49,810 --> 01:09:52,605
The third one is right around the corner.

1622
01:09:52,688 --> 01:09:55,232
- Yeah, it'll go up in the next round.
- It'll likely go back up.

1623
01:09:55,316 --> 01:09:56,567
I made 1,800 won.

1624
01:09:56,650 --> 01:09:58,652
- You made 1,800 won? That's a lot.
- That's more than 50%.

1625
01:09:58,736 --> 01:10:00,029
- That's a little over 50%, right?
- Yeah.

1626
01:10:00,112 --> 01:10:02,406
- That's a lot for sure.
- Sweet.

1627
01:10:06,619 --> 01:10:08,370
I'd like to buy Alt Ent's tip sheet.

1628
01:10:11,916 --> 01:10:14,752
DEALER ROOM

1629
01:10:14,835 --> 01:10:16,128
A 20% gain with NotSoGood Capital.

1630
01:10:16,212 --> 01:10:19,548
If I use Banger Steel
to earn some with Mucho Construction,

1631
01:10:19,632 --> 01:10:21,258
then I can keep cashing in on defense.

1632
01:10:22,218 --> 01:10:23,636
What's taking him so long?

1633
01:10:24,220 --> 01:10:25,846
A 20% gain with NotSoGood Capital.

1634
01:10:25,930 --> 01:10:28,933
I can block three,
and Alt Ent drops next round.

1635
01:10:29,016 --> 01:10:29,975
Won-young.

1636
01:10:30,059 --> 01:10:31,101
What's wrong?

1637
01:10:32,019 --> 01:10:32,978
What's up?

1638
01:10:37,358 --> 01:10:39,318
- I got the full answer.
- Okay.

1639
01:10:40,194 --> 01:10:42,196
"Alt Ent's stock price graph

1640
01:10:42,279 --> 01:10:44,406
matches the Mystery Stock Market icon."

1641
01:10:44,490 --> 01:10:45,532
- Icon?
- Really?

1642
01:10:45,616 --> 01:10:47,534
- The stock price.
- No way.

1643
01:10:47,618 --> 01:10:49,411
- It's gonna drop in the next round.
- It'll drop, then.

1644
01:10:49,495 --> 01:10:51,705
It only goes up once,
about five rounds later.

1645
01:10:51,789 --> 01:10:53,999
Who put the secret
on Analog Electronics this round?

1646
01:10:54,083 --> 01:10:56,961
- Shouldn't we buy Open Security?
- None of us did. They must've done it.

1647
01:10:57,044 --> 01:10:58,087
Shouldn't we go for Open Security?

1648
01:10:58,170 --> 01:10:59,838
- We should.
- Yeah.

1649
01:10:59,922 --> 01:11:01,465
It's so expensive now.

1650
01:11:01,548 --> 01:11:02,758
OPEN SECURITY: ▲26,842 WON

1651
01:11:09,265 --> 01:11:10,349
Well, he's busy.

1652
01:11:11,725 --> 01:11:13,310
- Shindong, come here.
- Are we set now?

1653
01:11:13,394 --> 01:11:14,270
No, no.

1654
01:11:14,353 --> 01:11:16,063
They're going after
NotSoGood Capital, right?

1655
01:11:16,146 --> 01:11:19,441
They were trying to
before you played them.

1656
01:11:19,525 --> 01:11:21,986
- Did it drop?
- Yeah.

1657
01:11:22,069 --> 01:11:24,321
Who put the secret on Analog Electronics?

1658
01:11:24,405 --> 01:11:25,781
It wasn't us.

1659
01:11:25,864 --> 01:11:27,032
I thought it was you guys.

1660
01:11:27,116 --> 01:11:28,242
- What's going on?
- Huh?

1661
01:11:28,325 --> 01:11:30,786
- No one knows.
- Save me.

1662
01:11:30,869 --> 01:11:32,288
Can I go for Open Security?

1663
01:11:32,371 --> 01:11:33,747
What?

1664
01:11:33,831 --> 01:11:35,708
- So…
- You know all the rules, right?

1665
01:11:35,791 --> 01:11:37,251
Be honest with me.

1666
01:11:37,960 --> 01:11:41,880
We just need to know if they're working
NotSoGood Capital and Banger Steel.

1667
01:11:41,964 --> 01:11:43,424
They failed, so it's over.

1668
01:11:43,507 --> 01:11:46,135
- So their op on NotSoGood Capital failed?
- Yeah, it's over.

1669
01:11:46,218 --> 01:11:47,594
But how do we know why it fell?

1670
01:11:47,678 --> 01:11:49,138
Because Mucho Construction went up.

1671
01:11:50,472 --> 01:11:52,308
Analog Electronics could've gone up, no?

1672
01:11:52,391 --> 01:11:54,560
No, Mucho Construction is the lowest.

1673
01:11:54,643 --> 01:11:56,603
You still don't know
NotSoGood Capital's rule, do you?

1674
01:11:56,687 --> 01:11:58,731
It relies on the movement
of more than half of the stocks.

1675
01:11:58,814 --> 01:12:00,357
- More than half of the stocks?
- Yeah.

1676
01:12:01,358 --> 01:12:02,318
No, it doesn't.

1677
01:12:03,235 --> 01:12:04,778
- Then?
- The lowest price.

1678
01:12:05,487 --> 01:12:08,324
- No, it's more than half.
- No, it's not.

1679
01:12:09,575 --> 01:12:12,036
Then who used a secret
on Analog Electronics?

1680
01:12:12,119 --> 01:12:12,953
Beats me.

1681
01:12:13,996 --> 01:12:14,872
I have no idea.

1682
01:12:16,790 --> 01:12:18,625
Damn it.

1683
01:12:18,709 --> 01:12:21,086
They said nobody over there used a secret.

1684
01:12:21,170 --> 01:12:22,921
Don't believe everything they say.

1685
01:12:23,005 --> 01:12:24,757
Oh, that's true. But--

1686
01:12:24,840 --> 01:12:27,384
- Stop going over there so much.
- They were so convincing.

1687
01:12:28,177 --> 01:12:30,512
<i>Round 16 will now begin.</i>

1688
01:12:30,596 --> 01:12:33,307
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

1689
01:12:33,932 --> 01:12:35,726
That stock is just straight money.

1690
01:12:35,809 --> 01:12:37,019
OPEN SECURITY: ▲30,331 WON

1691
01:12:37,686 --> 01:12:40,230
Analog Electronics
is really cheap right now.

1692
01:12:40,314 --> 01:12:41,940
- Is it?
- Yeah.

1693
01:12:42,024 --> 01:12:43,567
It might go up.

1694
01:12:43,650 --> 01:12:46,487
We can just buy info on Analog Electronics
and go from there.

1695
01:12:46,570 --> 01:12:47,905
- Buy the intel?
- Yeah.

1696
01:12:47,988 --> 01:12:50,032
- Analog Electronics.
- Would you like its intel?

1697
01:12:50,115 --> 01:12:51,450
Please submit a Piece.

1698
01:12:52,284 --> 01:12:53,827
Sorry, let me check that again.

1699
01:12:53,911 --> 01:12:55,788
"Total holdings between 10 and 30 shares…"

1700
01:12:57,748 --> 01:12:58,749
It's impossible.

1701
01:12:58,832 --> 01:13:01,460
Forget Analog Electronics.
The window is 10 to 30 shares.

1702
01:13:01,543 --> 01:13:03,212
- This part is "30 shares."
- Around 40,000 won.

1703
01:13:03,295 --> 01:13:04,463
Yeah, we make around that.

1704
01:13:04,546 --> 01:13:05,672
What do we buy, then?

1705
01:13:06,548 --> 01:13:07,966
Open Security.

1706
01:13:08,050 --> 01:13:10,302
- We have to buy Open Security again, huh?
- Yeah.

1707
01:13:10,386 --> 01:13:13,722
By the way, we need to profit
from Alt Ent one more time.

1708
01:13:13,806 --> 01:13:14,848
Keep that in mind.

1709
01:13:17,226 --> 01:13:20,062
ALT ENT: ▼3,700 WON

1710
01:13:20,145 --> 01:13:24,525
- So the third low point was 3,200 won.
- Right.

1711
01:13:24,608 --> 01:13:27,778
Check out the chart above.
The third low point is still up there.

1712
01:13:27,861 --> 01:13:30,280
- I think it can drop to about 1,500 won.
- Let's stay put in the next round.

1713
01:13:30,364 --> 01:13:32,157
- Maybe we can buy in the round after next.
- Yeah.

1714
01:13:37,704 --> 01:13:43,210
If we don't run trades on Banger Steel,
100 million won goes up in smoke.

1715
01:13:43,293 --> 01:13:44,503
- You're right.
- Yeah.

1716
01:13:44,586 --> 01:13:45,671
- We do need to do it.
- Yeah.

1717
01:13:45,754 --> 01:13:48,757
But the problem is we don't know
how much money the others have.

1718
01:13:48,841 --> 01:13:51,301
- So the secret needs to go.
- But to do that…

1719
01:13:51,385 --> 01:13:53,303
Once it's lifted… Check this out.

1720
01:13:53,387 --> 01:13:56,306
So, around Round 19,

1721
01:13:56,390 --> 01:13:59,435
we'll double our dough with Alt Ent
and then run the trades.

1722
01:13:59,518 --> 01:14:02,604
- Right, that's when the gap widens.
- Yeah.

1723
01:14:05,107 --> 01:14:06,358
Just remember that.

1724
01:14:09,445 --> 01:14:11,697
It's a bit late, but should we try
working on Banger Steel?

1725
01:14:11,780 --> 01:14:13,615
The last gamble.

1726
01:14:20,164 --> 01:14:22,207
Will the secret on Analog Electronics
expire now?

1727
01:14:22,291 --> 01:14:25,335
It'll still be in effect for this round,
so we can buy Open Security, no?

1728
01:14:25,419 --> 01:14:27,045
- You're right.
- It's based on the previous round?

1729
01:14:27,129 --> 01:14:29,131
- Yeah, it includes this round.
- I didn't know.

1730
01:14:29,214 --> 01:14:30,841
You should buy Security, Yurisa.

1731
01:14:30,924 --> 01:14:32,217
- Security?
- Yes, for 13%.

1732
01:14:32,301 --> 01:14:33,135
Open Security.

1733
01:14:33,677 --> 01:14:34,595
- Buy it?
- Yes.

1734
01:14:34,678 --> 01:14:36,221
- It's going up.
- Move up the rankings.

1735
01:14:37,014 --> 01:14:39,224
We need to get up in the rankings.

1736
01:14:39,308 --> 01:14:41,602
Do we have to work on
Banger Steel this round?

1737
01:14:41,685 --> 01:14:43,353
We need to buy at least four.

1738
01:14:43,437 --> 01:14:45,731
I should buy some more, just in case.

1739
01:14:45,814 --> 01:14:48,150
I bought six shares.

1740
01:14:48,233 --> 01:14:50,444
<i>That concludes Round 16.</i>

1741
01:14:50,527 --> 01:14:53,197
<i>Round 17 will now begin.</i>

1742
01:14:53,280 --> 01:14:56,033
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

1743
01:14:57,242 --> 01:14:59,536
- Yurisa, you bought Open Security, right?
- Yeah.

1744
01:14:59,620 --> 01:15:01,455
I did. I went all in.

1745
01:15:02,164 --> 01:15:05,083
This round, cash out Open Security shares.

1746
01:15:05,167 --> 01:15:07,836
We need to run trades on CoyoTech
and go all in on it.

1747
01:15:07,920 --> 01:15:11,340
Alt Ent bottoms out next round.

1748
01:15:11,423 --> 01:15:12,966
- Yeah.
- We'll buy it then. Let's get to work.

1749
01:15:13,050 --> 01:15:14,343
- On CoyoTech?
- Yeah.

1750
01:15:14,426 --> 01:15:17,804
- Analog Electronics--
- We had the worst luck with Capital.

1751
01:15:17,888 --> 01:15:19,890
- The strategy just failed, that's all.
- Yeah.

1752
01:15:19,973 --> 01:15:22,893
I didn't expect them to actually buy
when we put the secret on it.

1753
01:15:25,604 --> 01:15:27,856
- What now?
- What's wrong?

1754
01:15:28,440 --> 01:15:32,736
I was trying to gather information
from both sides

1755
01:15:32,819 --> 01:15:35,113
- and share it with you guys, but--
- Come on.

1756
01:15:35,197 --> 01:15:36,740
Come with us if you want.

1757
01:15:36,823 --> 01:15:38,951
- Go on.
- With the two-team situation…

1758
01:15:39,034 --> 01:15:41,203
- What?
- We got split into two teams,

1759
01:15:41,286 --> 01:15:43,205
and that put us in an awkward spot.

1760
01:15:43,288 --> 01:15:45,374
We couldn't just work
with the players in the living area.

1761
01:15:45,457 --> 01:15:50,629
I was trying to find a way to survive
once the rankings got solidified.

1762
01:15:50,712 --> 01:15:52,422
<i>I wanted to avoid going to prison</i>

1763
01:15:52,506 --> 01:15:54,508
<i>so I tried to see</i>
<i>if I could get an alliance token.</i>

1764
01:15:54,591 --> 01:15:57,886
So what's going on over there?

1765
01:15:57,970 --> 01:16:00,180
We've basically accepted
that we can't turn it around.

1766
01:16:00,264 --> 01:16:01,390
Right.

1767
01:16:01,473 --> 01:16:04,893
Yurisa, you should do something
to move up in the rankings.

1768
01:16:04,977 --> 01:16:06,103
How?

1769
01:16:11,066 --> 01:16:16,822
To be honest, Won-young played
really strangely on our team.

1770
01:16:16,905 --> 01:16:17,739
Right.

1771
01:16:18,323 --> 01:16:22,744
And I'm sure you know too,
but I feel like he lied to us yesterday.

1772
01:16:23,537 --> 01:16:27,666
Can't we just prevent them
from executing the Banger Steel play?

1773
01:16:27,749 --> 01:16:30,502
Just hold on to Banger Steel.
Selling it won't make it go up.

1774
01:16:30,586 --> 01:16:32,671
Alt Ent is the cheapest right now.

1775
01:16:32,754 --> 01:16:35,090
- NotSoGood Capital is gonna drop anyway.
- So Alt Ent…

1776
01:16:36,341 --> 01:16:38,051
- That's the cheapest.
- It doesn't affect us.

1777
01:16:38,135 --> 01:16:39,803
- That's right.
- Look.

1778
01:16:39,886 --> 01:16:42,306
I just bought ten shares of Banger Steel,

1779
01:16:42,389 --> 01:16:44,308
so you should buy Mucho Construction.

1780
01:16:44,391 --> 01:16:46,226
- Go all in on that.
- Wait, what doesn't affect us?

1781
01:16:46,310 --> 01:16:49,938
Won't NotSoGood Capital drop anyway
since Alt Ent is the cheapest?

1782
01:16:50,022 --> 01:16:54,276
He's saying that Alt Ent is gonna rise
in about two rounds.

1783
01:16:54,359 --> 01:16:57,821
You need to load up on Construction
and sell Open Security.

1784
01:16:57,904 --> 01:17:00,115
<i>That concludes Round 17.</i>

1785
01:17:00,657 --> 01:17:03,243
<i>Round 18 will now begin.</i>

1786
01:17:03,327 --> 01:17:06,038
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

1787
01:17:06,622 --> 01:17:08,790
- It's over, right?
- It is. We can't compete.

1788
01:17:08,874 --> 01:17:10,250
You went up in rankings.

1789
01:17:10,334 --> 01:17:12,502
- I know.
- You just need to keep it up.

1790
01:17:12,586 --> 01:17:18,091
11TH PLACE: SHINDONG
12TH PLACE: JUNG WON-YOUNG

1791
01:17:18,175 --> 01:17:20,969
- Go all in on Alt Ent this round.
- Okay.

1792
01:17:21,053 --> 01:17:23,472
Seok-jin, do you think
we should buy Alt Ent now

1793
01:17:23,555 --> 01:17:25,307
or wait one more round?

1794
01:17:25,390 --> 01:17:26,391
I think now.

1795
01:17:26,475 --> 01:17:28,310
Should we buy Alt Ent?

1796
01:17:28,393 --> 01:17:30,312
- I'm not sure.
- I think it's the next round.

1797
01:17:30,395 --> 01:17:32,272
I think it's the next.

1798
01:17:32,356 --> 01:17:34,608
It needs to do a little pivot first.

1799
01:17:35,442 --> 01:17:36,610
This is tough.

1800
01:17:37,611 --> 01:17:39,655
I guess I'll go for Alt Ent.

1801
01:17:39,738 --> 01:17:42,157
Wouldn't it be better
to invest in CoyoTech?

1802
01:17:43,533 --> 01:17:44,493
Are you going for Alt Ent?

1803
01:17:44,576 --> 01:17:46,995
They're not sure whether
this is the round to buy Alt Ent or not.

1804
01:17:47,079 --> 01:17:50,123
So they're going for CoyoTech instead.

1805
01:17:50,207 --> 01:17:52,417
COYOTECH: 24 SHARES

1806
01:17:52,501 --> 01:17:54,503
JAE JAE
COYOTECH: 15 SHARES BOUGHT

1807
01:17:54,586 --> 01:17:56,296
JOHN PARK
COYOTECH: 16 SHARES BOUGHT

1808
01:17:56,380 --> 01:17:58,507
What does your team wanna do now?

1809
01:17:58,590 --> 01:18:00,676
- You guys aren't exactly a team, right?
- We've got nothing.

1810
01:18:00,759 --> 01:18:03,261
We worked as a team
to get information on the rules.

1811
01:18:03,345 --> 01:18:05,847
What do you wanna do?
Just make as much money as you can?

1812
01:18:05,931 --> 01:18:08,433
I wanna know if the time for Alt Ent
is now or later.

1813
01:18:08,517 --> 01:18:11,103
The way I see the chart, it's now.

1814
01:18:14,314 --> 01:18:15,440
- I know that--
- What?

1815
01:18:15,524 --> 01:18:19,444
I know that Alt Ent will rise
after it hits the bend.

1816
01:18:19,528 --> 01:18:22,239
- Right.
- But I'm not sure if it's now or later.

1817
01:18:22,322 --> 01:18:23,156
- Is it the next round?
- It's now.

1818
01:18:23,240 --> 01:18:24,074
- Now?
- Yeah.

1819
01:18:24,157 --> 01:18:25,659
Hurry up and buy it.

1820
01:18:25,742 --> 01:18:27,744
<i>- That concludes Round 18.</i>
<i>- </i>I bought it.

1821
01:18:27,828 --> 01:18:29,121
Good.

1822
01:18:29,204 --> 01:18:31,289
<i>Round 19 will now begin.</i>

1823
01:18:31,373 --> 01:18:33,625
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

1824
01:18:33,709 --> 01:18:34,626
- What the…
- Huh?

1825
01:18:34,710 --> 01:18:36,169
ALT ENT: ▼1,000 WON

1826
01:18:36,253 --> 01:18:37,713
- I'm screwed.
- I'm screwed.

1827
01:18:37,796 --> 01:18:38,964
But why? Hold on.

1828
01:18:39,047 --> 01:18:39,881
Wait.

1829
01:18:41,508 --> 01:18:42,843
So it was the next round.

1830
01:18:43,427 --> 01:18:45,429
- I told you to go for CoyoTech.
- I know.

1831
01:18:45,512 --> 01:18:46,972
- We should've listened.
- Yeah.

1832
01:18:47,848 --> 01:18:49,349
Damn it.

1833
01:18:49,433 --> 01:18:51,935
Damn that icon. Unbelievable.

1834
01:18:52,018 --> 01:18:54,271
5TH PLACE: HYUN KYUNG-LYUL

1835
01:18:54,354 --> 01:18:56,398
- Thankfully, we're still in the top four.
- Yeah.

1836
01:18:56,481 --> 01:18:58,066
Everyone went for Alt Ent.

1837
01:18:58,150 --> 01:18:59,651
No, I don't think Kyung-lyul did.

1838
01:18:59,735 --> 01:19:00,736
- You're right.
- Yeah.

1839
01:19:00,819 --> 01:19:03,363
- You're going for Alt Ent, right?
- It's the way to go for this round.

1840
01:19:03,447 --> 01:19:04,740
- It'll probably double.
- Right.

1841
01:19:04,823 --> 01:19:08,076
Hold on, we're in trouble.
He's really catching up.

1842
01:19:08,160 --> 01:19:12,080
It's gonna be difficult
to add 100 million won at this rate.

1843
01:19:12,164 --> 01:19:14,374
- Dang it.
- Seriously.

1844
01:19:14,458 --> 01:19:16,460
- We messed up after all the work.
- That's how stocks are.

1845
01:19:16,543 --> 01:19:17,878
How did you jump up in the rankings?

1846
01:19:17,961 --> 01:19:19,212
Both stocks went up.

1847
01:19:19,296 --> 01:19:22,424
Mucho Construction and Banger Steel
suddenly went up.

1848
01:19:23,049 --> 01:19:24,676
Should I use a Piece?

1849
01:19:24,760 --> 01:19:27,053
If you wanna earn big,
now's your shot with Alt Ent.

1850
01:19:27,137 --> 01:19:30,182
- You're right.
- Yeah, it's time to gamble.

1851
01:19:30,682 --> 01:19:32,851
Would you like to exchange
your Piece for cash?

1852
01:19:32,934 --> 01:19:34,853
- Yes.
- How many would you like to exchange?

1853
01:19:34,936 --> 01:19:36,021
Two.

1854
01:19:36,104 --> 01:19:37,606
I'm going for one big swing.

1855
01:19:38,523 --> 01:19:39,441
On Alt Ent, sure.

1856
01:19:39,524 --> 01:19:41,818
No, I already took
the one big shot earlier.

1857
01:19:41,902 --> 01:19:44,446
Feels like I took a loan to average down.

1858
01:19:44,529 --> 01:19:47,032
So what are our team's goals now?

1859
01:19:47,115 --> 01:19:49,034
To claim the top four spots for us

1860
01:19:49,117 --> 01:19:51,328
and save Shindong somehow, right?

1861
01:19:51,411 --> 01:19:54,122
Who else are we gonna save?

1862
01:19:54,206 --> 01:19:55,791
What do you mean? That's it.

1863
01:19:55,874 --> 01:19:59,002
Aren't we helping Yurisa avoid last place?

1864
01:19:59,085 --> 01:20:00,921
Oh, yeah, we should do that.

1865
01:20:01,004 --> 01:20:02,422
Then what about Won-young?

1866
01:20:03,131 --> 01:20:04,716
- Regarding Yurisa and Won-young,
- Yes?

1867
01:20:05,342 --> 01:20:06,301
we should help them.

1868
01:20:06,384 --> 01:20:08,345
- Help them avoid last place. And?
- Yurisa…

1869
01:20:08,428 --> 01:20:11,014
But there's only so much we can do
after the discussion yesterday.

1870
01:20:11,097 --> 01:20:12,516
- Wait, Dong-min.
- Yeah?

1871
01:20:12,599 --> 01:20:16,728
<i>There isn't a big gap between</i>
<i>those in second through fifth place.</i>

1872
01:20:16,812 --> 01:20:19,397
That being said,
rankings could change at any moment,

1873
01:20:19,481 --> 01:20:21,066
and things will get complicated.

1874
01:20:24,152 --> 01:20:25,946
I need to place last.

1875
01:20:28,073 --> 01:20:30,492
Can you tell me
what the rule for Analog Electronics is?

1876
01:20:30,575 --> 01:20:32,369
- No idea.
- What do you mean you need to place last?

1877
01:20:32,452 --> 01:20:33,829
It's for the token.

1878
01:20:34,329 --> 01:20:36,039
Then you shouldn't place last.

1879
01:20:36,623 --> 01:20:37,791
Sorry, I can't tell you.

1880
01:20:38,291 --> 01:20:40,168
But you'd be eliminated.

1881
01:20:40,252 --> 01:20:43,588
- So you have to place last?
- Guess he got a mission yesterday.

1882
01:20:45,507 --> 01:20:48,510
- I knew it.
- So something happened yesterday, huh?

1883
01:20:48,593 --> 01:20:52,180
Then what did he come here to ask?
Was he just here to brag?

1884
01:20:56,393 --> 01:21:00,397
Won-young suddenly came by
and said he had to place last.

1885
01:21:00,480 --> 01:21:02,899
- He has to place last?
- Yes.

1886
01:21:02,983 --> 01:21:06,528
He's looking for ways to lower his assets.
He might just be acting.

1887
01:21:06,611 --> 01:21:11,741
But he could've easily come last
at any point if he wanted to.

1888
01:21:12,534 --> 01:21:15,662
It wouldn't make sense if he were told
to place last at a certain point.

1889
01:21:16,371 --> 01:21:18,248
Does it make any sense?

1890
01:21:18,331 --> 01:21:20,250
There's nothing easier
than coming in last.

1891
01:21:27,215 --> 01:21:30,886
Can anyone buy
around ten shares of Banger Steel?

1892
01:21:30,969 --> 01:21:32,345
- Banger Steel?
- Yes.

1893
01:21:32,429 --> 01:21:34,681
We can't use up our money yet.

1894
01:21:34,764 --> 01:21:36,182
You can't because you're first, right?

1895
01:21:37,058 --> 01:21:39,477
<i>That concludes Round 19.</i>

1896
01:21:39,561 --> 01:21:42,188
<i>Round 20 will now begin.</i>

1897
01:21:42,272 --> 01:21:46,818
<i>Here are the completed stock rules</i>
<i>and the updated stock prices.</i>

1898
01:21:47,527 --> 01:21:49,195
We were wrong about NotSoGood Capital.

1899
01:21:49,279 --> 01:21:52,657
It's not the most-dropped stock.
It's "four or more stocks."

1900
01:21:53,700 --> 01:21:55,160
Everyone will be after Alt Ent.

1901
01:21:55,660 --> 01:21:59,331
Everyone will go for Alt Ent.
The gap will just widen.

1902
01:21:59,414 --> 01:22:01,791
- There's no reason not to buy.
- Yeah, there isn't.

1903
01:22:02,500 --> 01:22:04,336
Wait, why did Shindong go down?

1904
01:22:05,503 --> 01:22:06,922
Why didn't you buy Alt Ent?

1905
01:22:07,005 --> 01:22:07,839
What?

1906
01:22:10,675 --> 01:22:12,135
It would've doubled if you did.

1907
01:22:12,802 --> 01:22:14,429
Yeah, why didn't you?

1908
01:22:14,512 --> 01:22:15,722
I told you to buy it.

1909
01:22:16,598 --> 01:22:17,891
I bought NotSoGood Capital.

1910
01:22:18,767 --> 01:22:20,393
- I'm such an idiot.
- Just buy it now.

1911
01:22:20,477 --> 01:22:23,939
Look, we can't be certain
because of Kyung-lyul.

1912
01:22:24,022 --> 01:22:26,608
We need to make more money
with another play.

1913
01:22:26,691 --> 01:22:29,819
That wouldn't be any fun.

1914
01:22:31,029 --> 01:22:33,239
- Isn't that obvious?
- There's no chance later.

1915
01:22:34,074 --> 01:22:37,035
- Now is the chance to go from 1,000 to 0.
- Alt Ent is the way to go.

1916
01:22:37,118 --> 01:22:38,244
What's going on here?

1917
01:22:38,328 --> 01:22:39,621
- The losers need to chat.
- So…

1918
01:22:39,704 --> 01:22:42,832
If we make the same investment,
he'll place last.

1919
01:22:42,916 --> 01:22:45,835
If we both go up, he'll still end up last.

1920
01:22:46,419 --> 01:22:47,420
Buy Alt Ent.

1921
01:22:48,880 --> 01:22:49,965
Hold on.

1922
01:22:50,048 --> 01:22:53,718
Our best option now is to stop them
from earning with NotSoGood Capital.

1923
01:22:53,802 --> 01:22:56,471
I'll spend some of my funds

1924
01:22:56,554 --> 01:22:58,765
- to buy Banger Steel--
- No, Dong-min.

1925
01:22:58,848 --> 01:23:03,478
Just wash trades on Analog Electronics
and buy 30 shares or more.

1926
01:23:03,561 --> 01:23:05,480
It only costs 31,000 won to get 31 shares.

1927
01:23:05,563 --> 01:23:08,191
- Why don't you buy 31 shares?
- Yeah, hold on to them.

1928
01:23:12,028 --> 01:23:13,321
- Can I come in?
- Sure.

1929
01:23:13,405 --> 01:23:15,281
- I want some snacks.
- Enjoy.

1930
01:23:21,121 --> 01:23:22,539
Analog Electronics…

1931
01:23:23,289 --> 01:23:24,874
Here you are.

1932
01:23:24,958 --> 01:23:25,834
Sorry?

1933
01:23:25,917 --> 01:23:27,961
I feel like I could make some money
with Analog Electronics,

1934
01:23:28,044 --> 01:23:29,462
but I could also be screwed over.

1935
01:23:30,171 --> 01:23:31,631
- Let me ask you one question.
- Yeah?

1936
01:23:31,715 --> 01:23:33,550
Is anyone on your team
gonna buy Electronics?

1937
01:23:33,633 --> 01:23:35,844
- I haven't mentioned anything about it.
- You haven't?

1938
01:23:35,927 --> 01:23:37,554
It's a gamble.

1939
01:23:41,224 --> 01:23:43,309
If I buy ten…

1940
01:23:43,893 --> 01:23:45,729
You wouldn't intentionally screw me over.

1941
01:23:45,812 --> 01:23:47,022
Why would I?

1942
01:23:49,065 --> 01:23:50,400
I just need to maintain my rank.

1943
01:23:51,067 --> 01:23:53,111
Let's do it.

1944
01:23:53,820 --> 01:23:55,030
Mucho Construction.

1945
01:23:56,448 --> 01:23:58,116
- Okay.
- All right.

1946
01:23:58,700 --> 01:24:01,036
I'll buy 16 more.

1947
01:24:01,703 --> 01:24:04,706
You should eat up now
if you're headed to prison.

1948
01:24:04,789 --> 01:24:07,167
<i>That concludes Round 20.</i>

1949
01:24:07,250 --> 01:24:09,627
<i>Round 21 will now begin.</i>

1950
01:24:10,128 --> 01:24:12,922
<i>Here are the updated stock prices.</i>

1951
01:24:13,006 --> 01:24:14,466
11TH PLACE: JUNG WON-YOUNG
12TH PLACE: SHINDONG

1952
01:24:14,549 --> 01:24:15,717
What happened to Shindong?

1953
01:24:16,509 --> 01:24:18,553
What's going on?

1954
01:24:19,304 --> 01:24:20,513
What happened to Shindong?

1955
01:24:21,556 --> 01:24:22,807
How does that make sense?

1956
01:24:25,769 --> 01:24:27,187
What did you do?

1957
01:24:29,397 --> 01:24:31,149
I'll buy 16 more.

1958
01:24:31,232 --> 01:24:32,609
I need to place last.

1959
01:24:32,692 --> 01:24:34,069
Load up on Construction
and sell Open Security.

1960
01:24:34,152 --> 01:24:35,320
You should buy Security, Yurisa.

1961
01:24:35,403 --> 01:24:36,780
The last gamble.

1962
01:24:36,863 --> 01:24:38,490
I bought Banger Steel and blocked it.

1963
01:24:38,573 --> 01:24:40,450
Sorry, but can I buy CoyoTech?

1964
01:24:40,533 --> 01:24:41,868
Go for Analog Electronics.

1965
01:24:41,951 --> 01:24:43,453
I've only been working with Shindong.

1966
01:24:43,536 --> 01:24:45,455
I wanna buy a share of NotSoGood Capital.

1967
01:24:45,538 --> 01:24:52,545
15 HOURS AGO

1968
01:24:53,505 --> 01:24:56,007
<i>To break the curse,</i>

1969
01:24:56,633 --> 01:24:59,969
<i>the one player you choose</i>

1970
01:25:00,053 --> 01:25:05,016
<i>must be eliminated</i>
<i>in tomorrow's main match.</i>

1971
01:25:12,190 --> 01:25:16,945
<i>Who do you choose</i>
<i>as the player to be eliminated tomorrow?</i>

1972
01:25:20,532 --> 01:25:22,075
I choose Shindong.

1973
01:27:00,089 --> 01:27:05,094
Subtitle translation by: Justin S. Kim
